WEBVTT


00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:04.250
High school.


00:01:05.333 --> 00:01:07.411
Look familiar? Yeah.


00:01:09.300 --> 00:01:11.551
Being a teenager,
it can be rough,


00:01:11.618 --> 00:01:13.320
I'm not gonna
lie to you.


00:01:13.388 --> 00:01:16.973
But if you're a teenager,
and the world doesn't fit you,


00:01:17.041 --> 00:01:18.175
you're totally hosed!


00:01:19.410 --> 00:01:21.111
# Oh, Mr. Pit...
Oh, Mr. Pit...


00:01:21.179 --> 00:01:22.562
# Mr. Pitiful


00:01:22.864 --> 00:01:24.748
# Who let you down?


00:01:27.351 --> 00:01:29.203
# Who let you down?
Who let you down?


00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.188
And the harder
you try to fit in,


00:01:31.255 --> 00:01:32.990
the more awkward it gets.


00:01:33.057 --> 00:01:34.974
# Oh, Mr. Pit...
Oh, Mr. Pit...


00:01:35.043 --> 00:01:36.760
# Mr. Pitiful


00:01:36.828 --> 00:01:38.094
# Who let you down?


00:01:38.162 --> 00:01:39.696
Look at this poor guy.


00:01:39.764 --> 00:01:41.297
Brutal!


00:01:41.365 --> 00:01:44.167
# Who let you down?
Who let you down? #


00:01:44.235 --> 00:01:46.369
But if you think
being a big, awkward teenager


00:01:46.437 --> 00:01:48.838
is about the worst thing
that can happen to you,


00:01:48.906 --> 00:01:51.741
try being
a 200-pound teenage dog


00:01:51.809 --> 00:01:54.160
with a radar dish
wrapped around your neck!


00:01:54.228 --> 00:01:56.814
Oh, yeah, that'll make me
real popular.


00:01:56.881 --> 00:02:00.316
Luckily, they're easy
to take off. Watch this.


00:02:00.384 --> 00:02:02.202
Marmaduke!
Told you!


00:02:02.269 --> 00:02:03.303
Where are you?


00:02:03.371 --> 00:02:05.072
Hold your horses.


00:02:05.139 --> 00:02:08.007
I'm Marmaduke, by the way.
I get yelled at a lot.


00:02:08.076 --> 00:02:10.210
Come on, let's meet the fam.
The two-leggers.


00:02:10.278 --> 00:02:11.545
You're gonna love them.


00:02:11.612 --> 00:02:13.280
Here I come!


00:02:15.282 --> 00:02:18.384
This little Padawan here
is Brian.


00:02:18.452 --> 00:02:21.438
Like most kids his age,
he loves to hang out with me.


00:02:21.506 --> 00:02:24.374
Come on, buddy.
I can't see!


00:02:24.442 --> 00:02:27.711
Yeah, I'm pretty busy myself.
I'll catch you later.


00:02:27.778 --> 00:02:30.214
And this social
butterfly here is Barbara.


00:02:30.281 --> 00:02:31.949
She loves to
play ball with me.


00:02:32.016 --> 00:02:34.334
Okay, Barb,
you throw and I catch.


00:02:34.402 --> 00:02:35.885
He can be like that.


00:02:35.953 --> 00:02:36.887
Not like that.


00:02:36.954 --> 00:02:38.121
Is somebody cooking?


00:02:38.622 --> 00:02:40.139
Food!


00:02:40.207 --> 00:02:42.876
Debbie's pretty cool,
and my main food hook-up.


00:02:42.944 --> 00:02:46.263
She slips me a steak here,
some turkey there.


00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:50.166
Which is why I think she doesn't
even care when I help myself.


00:02:50.434 --> 00:02:52.469
Come to daddy.


00:02:52.537 --> 00:02:54.988
Ahhh! Hot cheese!
Oh, hot cheese!


00:02:57.958 --> 00:02:59.259
Marmaduke!


00:03:01.529 --> 00:03:02.979
The little one's Sarah.


00:03:03.047 --> 00:03:06.182
How cute is she?
And she's my biggest fan.


00:03:06.251 --> 00:03:08.618
You know, it's important for
them to get exercise at this age,


00:03:08.686 --> 00:03:10.753
so I try to take her
for a walk every day.


00:03:11.723 --> 00:03:14.341
She's got a great laugh,
doesn't she?


00:03:14.408 --> 00:03:15.859
Then there's
my owner, Phil.


00:03:15.894 --> 00:03:18.462
He's a marketing guy for
a local pet food company.


00:03:18.529 --> 00:03:20.096
I call him
Doctor No sometimes,


00:03:20.164 --> 00:03:22.132
'cause it's nothing
but rules with him.


00:03:22.199 --> 00:03:23.500
No slobbering.


00:03:23.568 --> 00:03:26.270
No barking.
No tackling the mailman.


00:03:26.337 --> 00:03:29.088
Here, let's see if he says no
to this awesome hole I'm digging.


00:03:29.156 --> 00:03:30.656
Marmaduke, no!


00:03:30.724 --> 00:03:34.327
See? Doctor No
in the house.


00:03:34.362 --> 00:03:36.212
Why don't you just
give it a chance?


00:03:37.415 --> 00:03:39.932
I will find China!


00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.437
What you're doing
is cruel and unusual.


00:03:44.505 --> 00:03:46.272
I hate water.
Come on. Sit.


00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:47.741
Look, everybody's got a weakness. Sit.


00:03:47.808 --> 00:03:50.109
Mine's water. It's my kryptonite. Sit.


00:03:50.177 --> 00:03:53.212
Not sitting in this tub.
Sit, sit, sit.


00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:55.215
Sit, Marmaduke!


00:03:55.283 --> 00:03:57.551
What can I say? I'm
a sucker for the kid.


00:03:57.751 --> 00:03:59.002
Bye-bye.


00:03:59.070 --> 00:04:00.971
Phil hates that.


00:04:01.038 --> 00:04:02.305
Hey, Sarah,
where you going?


00:04:02.373 --> 00:04:03.873
Stay.


00:04:03.941 --> 00:04:08.311
There's nothing good about
getting a bath, except for this!


00:04:08.379 --> 00:04:10.030
Come on, Phil!
Not again.


00:04:10.097 --> 00:04:11.364
Marmaduke!


00:04:11.399 --> 00:04:12.733
Let's go!


00:04:12.800 --> 00:04:14.117
Marmaduke!


00:04:14.185 --> 00:04:16.002
I like to give Phil
a little exercise, too.


00:04:16.037 --> 00:04:19.455
He's cooped up in the office
all day. Come on, Phil.


00:04:19.540 --> 00:04:21.158
That's the spirit!
Get back here!


00:04:21.225 --> 00:04:22.342
Over here!


00:04:22.410 --> 00:04:25.395
Come here, through here,
Phil! I'm over here!


00:04:25.462 --> 00:04:26.963
Yeah, come on!


00:04:28.065 --> 00:04:30.283
Not this time...


00:04:30.351 --> 00:04:32.035
You don't grab a tiger
by the tail!


00:04:35.156 --> 00:04:36.206
Marmaduke!


00:04:36.274 --> 00:04:38.508
Someone call the ASPCA!


00:04:38.575 --> 00:04:40.860
We got a crazy dog
on the loose!


00:04:40.928 --> 00:04:42.529
Freedom!


00:04:46.484 --> 00:04:48.418
Hey, Dad.
What are you doing?


00:04:50.154 --> 00:04:53.373
Would it kill them
to install a new dog door?


00:04:53.440 --> 00:04:56.142
I was two months old
when they got this.


00:04:56.210 --> 00:05:00.113
I guess I had more pull before
the growth spurt. Cue flashback.


00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:01.415
Oh, he's so cute!


00:05:01.482 --> 00:05:04.550
See? Insanely cute.


00:05:04.618 --> 00:05:06.786
Look at that lovable
little Marma-pup.


00:05:06.788 --> 00:05:08.989
Come here, you!


00:05:09.156 --> 00:05:12.959
But when you grow up into
this, I get it. Not pretty.


00:05:13.027 --> 00:05:14.661
I'd ignore me, too.
Get back here!


00:05:14.729 --> 00:05:16.730
Hey, I'm talking here!


00:05:18.549 --> 00:05:21.318
Anyway, I try not to
hold things against Phil.


00:05:21.386 --> 00:05:23.120
After all,
he's only human.


00:05:23.187 --> 00:05:27.491
That's why I make it a point
to never go to bed hungry.


00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:28.942
Let's see
what we've got.


00:05:29.010 --> 00:05:30.811
Sausage from
last week's barbecue,


00:05:30.878 --> 00:05:32.896
gonna need to let that
breathe a few days.


00:05:32.963 --> 00:05:36.966
This is our shot.
California, the big leagues.


00:05:37.034 --> 00:05:40.303
In the big leagues, they take
steroids and cheat with supermodels.


00:05:40.338 --> 00:05:42.972
It's a marketing job with
an organic pet food company.


00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:44.840
I think we'll be okay.


00:05:44.908 --> 00:05:47.260
Pepperoni pizza.


00:05:47.327 --> 00:05:49.696
Phil's loafer? No, I'll
save it for dessert.


00:05:49.764 --> 00:05:52.565
And that, I have no idea what that is.


00:05:52.633 --> 00:05:54.617
Aren't we okay
in Kansas?


00:05:54.685 --> 00:05:58.221
Is that what we wanna be? Just okay?


00:05:58.289 --> 00:05:59.656
Coming in for a landing.


00:05:59.724 --> 00:06:01.758
I wanna give you and the
kids the life you deserve.


00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:04.310
I want a bigger house


00:06:04.378 --> 00:06:06.262
with a bedroom that doesn't
smell like a meat-locker.


00:06:08.633 --> 00:06:11.017
This is our shot.


00:06:11.084 --> 00:06:14.453
Well, if this is our shot,
then we should take it.


00:06:14.522 --> 00:06:16.823
But you have to
tell the kids.


00:06:16.891 --> 00:06:17.907
Done.


00:06:19.193 --> 00:06:20.226
Give me that.


00:06:20.294 --> 00:06:21.911
Oh! Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:06:21.946 --> 00:06:23.463
Hey, I wasn't done
with that!


00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:26.950
You don't have to worry, I've
got my supermodel right here.


00:06:27.018 --> 00:06:28.935
Wow!


00:06:29.003 --> 00:06:32.005
Wait for it...
Wait for it...


00:06:33.273 --> 00:06:34.741
Marmaduke!
Marmaduke!


00:06:34.809 --> 00:06:36.560
What did you eat?


00:06:38.913 --> 00:06:42.048
I know it's juvenile,
but it's all I've got.


00:06:42.115 --> 00:06:43.315
So, there you have it.


00:06:43.383 --> 00:06:45.518
Day in the life of
old Marmaduke, here.


00:06:45.586 --> 00:06:46.820
It's really bad!


00:06:46.887 --> 00:06:47.987
Guys, I am sorry.


00:06:48.022 --> 00:06:50.640
That was a little much,
even for me.


00:06:50.707 --> 00:06:51.907
Bad Marmaduke.


00:06:51.975 --> 00:06:54.244
All right, enough.
Lights out.


00:06:58.849 --> 00:07:02.068
Waffles, waffles,
waffles, waffles, waffles!


00:07:02.503 --> 00:07:04.003
Yes!


00:07:04.071 --> 00:07:06.323
Saturday morning waffles!
Got to love the Debster!


00:07:06.390 --> 00:07:07.890
Take it easy, man!


00:07:07.959 --> 00:07:10.659
A waffle is to be
savored, not inhaled!


00:07:10.694 --> 00:07:12.562
Hey, this is my step-bro,
Carlos, by the way.


00:07:12.630 --> 00:07:14.297
Say hey, Carlos.
Hey, Carlos.


00:07:14.364 --> 00:07:16.282
He's pretty cool
for a cat, which helps,


00:07:16.349 --> 00:07:19.285
since he's basically
my only friend.


00:07:19.370 --> 00:07:20.871
You ready for
a bombshell?


00:07:20.938 --> 00:07:21.854
Lay it on me.


00:07:21.922 --> 00:07:24.508
Phil just told everybody
he got a new job.


00:07:24.575 --> 00:07:26.176
We're moving
to the O.C.!


00:07:26.243 --> 00:07:28.144
Shut up! Really?


00:07:28.179 --> 00:07:31.864
No lie! I was so shocked,
I hacked that thing up.


00:07:31.933 --> 00:07:34.351
Carlos, that's gross!


00:07:34.418 --> 00:07:36.052
I know it's gonna take
time to adjust, honey,


00:07:36.119 --> 00:07:38.621
but you'll make so many
new friends there.


00:07:38.689 --> 00:07:40.707
I think it sounds
kind of cool.


00:07:40.775 --> 00:07:42.876
What do you care? All you
do is play video games.


00:07:42.944 --> 00:07:44.243
This is so unfair!


00:07:44.311 --> 00:07:45.912
I got to say,
I'm with Barbara on this one.


00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:48.414
You know how many bones
I buried in the backyard?


00:07:48.482 --> 00:07:51.268
Guys, this is a
once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.


00:07:51.335 --> 00:07:54.386
We'll have a big new house
with a pool and a company car.


00:07:59.677 --> 00:08:02.011
Pets are always
the last to find out!


00:08:02.079 --> 00:08:04.614
I don't even know
where the O.C.'s at!


00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.168
Okay, what's the deal?
Is it something I said?


00:08:09.169 --> 00:08:11.938
Something you weren't
supposed to say.


00:08:12.005 --> 00:08:14.407
Does anyone even own
a pet in this place?


00:08:14.474 --> 00:08:17.010
I haven't seen
a single dog so far.


00:08:17.077 --> 00:08:18.794
It's kind of hard to forgive
you if you don't mean it...


00:08:18.862 --> 00:08:20.513
Oh! She's fine.


00:08:20.580 --> 00:08:23.616
Okay, so far, all I've
learned about The O.C. is that


00:08:23.684 --> 00:08:27.219
no one has a pet and Seth,
here, is a total drama queen.


00:08:27.287 --> 00:08:29.455
You're the biggest
drama queen, amigo.


00:08:29.523 --> 00:08:31.557
Me?
That's you, Carlos.


00:08:31.625 --> 00:08:34.894
You're, like, 200 pounds
of drama, with a red collar!


00:08:34.962 --> 00:08:37.596
Oh, really?
This conversation is over.


00:08:37.665 --> 00:08:38.698
No, no, no!


00:08:40.601 --> 00:08:42.836
Ejector seat.
Never fails.


00:08:44.572 --> 00:08:47.173
And so,
moving day arrived.


00:08:47.240 --> 00:08:48.942
And there was
a feeling of hope


00:08:49.009 --> 00:08:51.077
and excitement for
the whole family.


00:08:51.144 --> 00:08:53.780
Even Barbara was trying
to lend a hand.


00:08:53.848 --> 00:08:55.348
That's mine...


00:08:55.415 --> 00:08:56.732
Carlos and I would
have pitched in, too,


00:08:56.767 --> 00:09:00.737
but we were being
shipped air freight and on lockdown!


00:09:00.804 --> 00:09:02.955
Hey, let me out of here.
I'm not an animal!


00:09:04.658 --> 00:09:05.758
Oh, yeah, I am.


00:09:05.826 --> 00:09:09.746
Look what I got.
Debbie's meatballs!


00:09:09.814 --> 00:09:11.230
That's my man, Phil!


00:09:11.298 --> 00:09:12.782
There you go.


00:09:12.849 --> 00:09:15.351
Looking out
for his own.


00:09:15.419 --> 00:09:18.154
I don't know, Carlos.
Something's fishy here.


00:09:18.222 --> 00:09:20.673
It's Debbie's
meatballs, man. Don't question it!


00:09:20.708 --> 00:09:23.592
Oh! I know I shouldn't eat
it, but I can't help it.


00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:26.462
Good boy! Good boy!


00:09:27.665 --> 00:09:29.532
Oh, yeah. Oh, yeah.


00:09:35.022 --> 00:09:37.556
I feel a little funny.


00:09:37.624 --> 00:09:39.575
This is
a horrible mistake.


00:09:39.610 --> 00:09:41.527
I requested
executive class!


00:09:41.595 --> 00:09:44.697
I think Phil put something
in our meatballs!


00:09:44.765 --> 00:09:47.734
Have you ever
looked at your paws?


00:09:47.801 --> 00:09:50.469
I mean,
really looked at them?


00:09:50.537 --> 00:09:53.439
Yeah, yeah. I followed
you on many adventures.


00:09:53.507 --> 00:09:57.744
But into the great unknown
mystery, I will go first, amigo.


00:09:57.811 --> 00:09:58.628
Timber!


00:09:59.963 --> 00:10:01.814
Down and out.


00:10:07.070 --> 00:10:10.206
# California, here we come


00:10:10.273 --> 00:10:13.425
# Right back
where we started from


00:10:13.493 --> 00:10:14.961
# California!


00:10:15.029 --> 00:10:21.984
# California! #


00:10:24.855 --> 00:10:26.272
Wake up! I'm up, I'm up!
Come on, Phil, let's do it!


00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.875
Same dog, different floor.


00:10:28.943 --> 00:10:33.012
Yes! New city,
new house, new smells!


00:10:34.198 --> 00:10:37.400
Good morning,
Orange County!


00:10:39.136 --> 00:10:40.704
Oh, yeah.


00:10:40.771 --> 00:10:43.440
Hang on a second. Did you
check out that doggie door?


00:10:43.507 --> 00:10:47.577
It fits! It fits!
Oh! Look at this.


00:10:47.645 --> 00:10:50.913
It's got an ocean view!
And a pool!


00:10:50.981 --> 00:10:52.699
This grass is so green!


00:10:54.234 --> 00:10:57.570
And this, by far, the nicest
bathroom I've ever had.


00:10:57.638 --> 00:10:59.788
Speaking of which,
a little privacy, please.


00:11:02.459 --> 00:11:05.194
Oh, yeah, brown collar. Good,
that'll bring out my eyes.


00:11:05.262 --> 00:11:06.829
Come on, Phil, let's go!


00:11:06.897 --> 00:11:09.399
Is that weird that your boss
wants to meet you at the dog park?


00:11:09.466 --> 00:11:11.066
That's how
they roll in Cali.


00:11:11.134 --> 00:11:13.603
Don's a bit eccentric, but that's
what makes him so successful.


00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:15.070
Come on, Phil, shake a leg! Easy, buddy!


00:11:15.138 --> 00:11:16.339
Wait.
Pink?


00:11:16.407 --> 00:11:18.458
Fuchsia. That's how
they roll in Cali.


00:11:18.526 --> 00:11:19.975
Come on,
we're burning daylight.


00:11:20.043 --> 00:11:21.661
Let's do it! Don't worry
about me, I'll just be here


00:11:21.728 --> 00:11:23.863
unpacking a thousand boxes.


00:11:23.931 --> 00:11:24.880
Freedom!


00:11:24.948 --> 00:11:26.383
I promise I'll be
home early to help!


00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:27.584
Let's go!


00:11:28.385 --> 00:11:30.487
That's the company car?


00:11:31.522 --> 00:11:32.638
# California


00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:35.341
# knows how to party


00:11:35.376 --> 00:11:37.744
# California


00:11:37.811 --> 00:11:40.596
# knows how to party


00:11:40.664 --> 00:11:44.166
# In the city of L.A.


00:11:44.234 --> 00:11:48.271
We are
living the dream, Phil!


00:11:48.338 --> 00:11:50.439
# We keep it rockin'! #


00:11:51.609 --> 00:11:53.209
Listen, big guy.


00:11:53.277 --> 00:11:54.977
Things are gonna work a little
different out here. Give me those.


00:11:55.045 --> 00:11:56.112
Hey, that's part
of my look!


00:11:56.179 --> 00:11:57.447
We need to impress
my new boss.


00:11:57.515 --> 00:12:00.983
I need you to be a good
boy, a very good boy.


00:12:01.051 --> 00:12:03.319
Basically,
the opposite of you.


00:12:03.387 --> 00:12:05.905
Hi. Morning!


00:12:05.972 --> 00:12:09.842
Phil's got nothing to worry
about. Why? Twelve simple words.


00:12:09.910 --> 00:12:13.212
I've got a chance to completely
re-invent myself and finally fit in.


00:12:13.280 --> 00:12:16.182
In short, I've got
a new leash on life.


00:12:17.551 --> 00:12:19.118
Pun intended.


00:12:21.455 --> 00:12:24.190
Wow, this is
Phil's office?


00:12:25.893 --> 00:12:28.861
New life, here I come.


00:12:28.929 --> 00:12:30.980
Time to bring my A-game.


00:12:31.231 --> 00:12:34.751
Think small, play it
cool, get your bark on.


00:12:34.819 --> 00:12:37.603
Just relax.
Hey, how's it going?


00:12:37.671 --> 00:12:38.638
Beautiful day, huh?


00:12:38.705 --> 00:12:39.906
Oh, hey, cool sweater!


00:12:39.973 --> 00:12:41.807
I'm sweating like a dog.


00:12:41.875 --> 00:12:43.543
Come on, big M,
keep it together.


00:12:43.611 --> 00:12:47.212
Just focus. Whoa!
What was that? Whoa!


00:12:47.280 --> 00:12:48.698
Cool it!
Hey, wait for me.


00:12:48.766 --> 00:12:49.899
Marmaduke, heel!


00:12:49.967 --> 00:12:51.301
Phil, wait, wait,
check it out!


00:12:51.336 --> 00:12:53.686
Winslow, here.


00:12:53.754 --> 00:12:55.454
Oh, Mr. Twombly,
there you are.


00:12:55.522 --> 00:12:57.190
It's great to
see you again.


00:12:57.257 --> 00:12:58.224
Who do we have here?


00:12:58.292 --> 00:12:59.325
Come on, buddy!


00:13:00.027 --> 00:13:01.194
Yeah! What's his name?


00:13:01.262 --> 00:13:03.112
This is Marmaduke.
Marmaduke!


00:13:03.147 --> 00:13:06.299
Well, you are one handsome
Great Dane, you know that?


00:13:06.366 --> 00:13:08.250
I'm starting to
like this guy!


00:13:08.318 --> 00:13:10.703
You've got yourself a beautiful
best friend there, Phil.


00:13:10.771 --> 00:13:13.689
Thank you! Marmaduke and I,
we're like two peas in a pod.


00:13:13.757 --> 00:13:14.807
Hmm.


00:13:14.875 --> 00:13:16.709
Who's licking butt now?


00:13:16.744 --> 00:13:17.960
Interesting.


00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:22.832
I'm picking up something
else here, also.


00:13:23.734 --> 00:13:25.802
Absolutely not a purebred.


00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.269
Really?


00:13:27.505 --> 00:13:30.957
I'm sensing a little
English Mastiff.


00:13:31.025 --> 00:13:32.842
Hey, watch it!


00:13:32.909 --> 00:13:34.510
Your guess is
as good as mine.


00:13:37.398 --> 00:13:39.732
You don't know your own
best friend, Phil?


00:13:39.767 --> 00:13:41.133
Sure. Uh...


00:13:41.719 --> 00:13:43.486
I love dogs.


00:13:43.554 --> 00:13:46.689
I can tell a lot about a man
by the way he treats his dog.


00:13:47.725 --> 00:13:50.226
That's why I like
working out here.


00:13:50.293 --> 00:13:54.230
I can measure, first-hand,
who I'm dealing with.


00:13:56.984 --> 00:13:58.618
Watch it, Phil.
He can smell your fear.


00:13:58.685 --> 00:14:02.372
Plus, you get all this fresh
air for out-of-the-box thinking.


00:14:02.439 --> 00:14:06.509
And, most importantly, I get to
spend time with my little girl.


00:14:07.311 --> 00:14:08.494
Jezebel.


00:14:09.914 --> 00:14:12.115
Oh!


00:14:12.182 --> 00:14:14.066
Hello, Cali!


00:14:16.052 --> 00:14:18.020
Look at that fur!


00:14:19.173 --> 00:14:21.740
Right. Take off your
shoes and let's walk.


00:14:21.808 --> 00:14:23.242
You don't wear
shoes out here?


00:14:23.310 --> 00:14:26.045
Come on, Phil.
Channel your inner canine.


00:14:26.112 --> 00:14:28.514
Get some earth
between your toes.


00:14:28.582 --> 00:14:31.851
It's not the earth
I'm worried about.


00:14:31.918 --> 00:14:33.486
Stay out of trouble.
Good luck, Phil.


00:14:33.553 --> 00:14:34.753
You're gonna need it.


00:14:35.505 --> 00:14:38.557
Jezebel! Whoa!


00:14:39.726 --> 00:14:41.644
Hey, whoa, whoa.
Watch it!


00:14:41.712 --> 00:14:43.396
Bakersfield.
What the...


00:14:43.463 --> 00:14:44.696
He's definitely Midwest.


00:14:44.764 --> 00:14:46.682
Boston?
I'm gonna say Kansas.


00:14:46.750 --> 00:14:48.117
How did you know?


00:14:48.184 --> 00:14:51.153
It's a gift.
What's your handle, newbie?


00:14:51.221 --> 00:14:52.204
My name's Marmaduke.


00:14:52.239 --> 00:14:55.040
Yikes!
Immediately moving on.


00:14:55.108 --> 00:14:56.242
Meet the gang.


00:14:56.310 --> 00:14:58.010
The egghead, here,
is Raisin.


00:14:58.078 --> 00:14:59.211
Marmaduke.


00:14:59.279 --> 00:15:01.147
A unique synthesis
of "marma",


00:15:01.214 --> 00:15:04.083
the scientific name for
the jumping spider family...


00:15:04.151 --> 00:15:05.885
Oh! Oh!
I hate spiders.


00:15:05.953 --> 00:15:07.486
...and the Duke
of Marlborough,


00:15:07.554 --> 00:15:09.689
the 17th-century
English statesman.


00:15:09.756 --> 00:15:12.976
And the ultra-confident Chinese
Crested over here is Giuseppe.


00:15:13.043 --> 00:15:17.347
Before you ask, yes, I'm a real
dog. No, I'm not a chew toy.


00:15:17.414 --> 00:15:21.234
And I just get a little nervous
sometimes because we live in California.


00:15:21.301 --> 00:15:22.818
This is the land
of the puma!


00:15:22.820 --> 00:15:25.104
There are no pumas
in Southern California.


00:15:25.172 --> 00:15:28.006
Pumas!
They come out of nowhere.


00:15:29.893 --> 00:15:31.644
I'm Mazie, by the way.


00:15:31.711 --> 00:15:34.447
Good to meet you guys.
Hey, you come here a lot?


00:15:34.514 --> 00:15:37.950
It's the dog park, man. It's
like high school for dogs,


00:15:38.017 --> 00:15:40.352
which means there's a
few packs to know about.


00:15:41.404 --> 00:15:43.473
First,
you got your jocks.


00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:45.091
Nice catch, Brad.


00:15:45.158 --> 00:15:47.309
The only muscle they
don't use is their brain.


00:15:47.377 --> 00:15:48.844
O- M-G, Brad is H-O-T!


00:15:48.912 --> 00:15:51.347
They mostly date Afghans.
Who actually have no brain.


00:15:51.414 --> 00:15:52.881
Oh! Frisbee!


00:15:52.949 --> 00:15:55.384
Then you got
your drama geeks.


00:15:55.451 --> 00:15:56.986
We're innocent.
Don't shoot!


00:15:57.054 --> 00:15:58.688
Bang, bang.


00:15:58.755 --> 00:16:01.123
And over here,
your mushroom heads.


00:16:01.191 --> 00:16:05.328
Somebody stop this thing,
man. I got to get off, bro!


00:16:05.395 --> 00:16:08.314
Then there's your out-and-out
juvenile delinquents.


00:16:10.567 --> 00:16:12.602
Come on! Let's go, go!


00:16:12.669 --> 00:16:15.905
Word to the wise,
avoid the water bowls here.


00:16:15.973 --> 00:16:18.240
Oh, come on! Again?


00:16:20.393 --> 00:16:23.395
So far, I'm not seeing
anyone I'd really fit in with.


00:16:23.464 --> 00:16:26.532
Well, if you think you got the
game, you could roll with our crew.


00:16:26.600 --> 00:16:28.184
Oh, yeah?
Who's your crew?


00:16:28.252 --> 00:16:29.268
Mutts!
Mutts!


00:16:30.470 --> 00:16:31.970
Weird!


00:16:32.923 --> 00:16:34.056
Who are those guys?


00:16:34.124 --> 00:16:36.525
The pedigrees,
a.k.a. trouble.


00:16:36.593 --> 00:16:38.578
They're
rich, and they're spoiled


00:16:38.645 --> 00:16:41.347
and they act like their fleas
don't bite. It's ridiculous!


00:16:41.382 --> 00:16:44.884
The little land shrimps
are Thunder and Lightning.


00:16:44.952 --> 00:16:48.071
Dog Vader over there
is the man himself, Bosco.


00:16:48.138 --> 00:16:49.504
Alpha male
who runs the park.


00:16:49.572 --> 00:16:51.240
He's the toughest
dog around.


00:16:51.307 --> 00:16:54.544
Him? He
doesn't look that tough.


00:16:54.611 --> 00:16:57.946
His girlfriend over there
is Miss Perfect, Jezebel.


00:16:58.014 --> 00:16:59.214
And he's super-jealous,


00:16:59.282 --> 00:17:01.234
so stay away from her
or he'll turn you into...


00:17:01.301 --> 00:17:02.868
Dog food.


00:17:02.936 --> 00:17:04.854
Hello, losers.


00:17:04.922 --> 00:17:06.588
Speak of the devil.


00:17:06.656 --> 00:17:08.541
So, I see you got
a new mutt friend.


00:17:08.609 --> 00:17:10.242
Okay, that's wet.


00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:12.044
Shut up, Thunder.


00:17:12.129 --> 00:17:13.479
What's his name?


00:17:13.546 --> 00:17:16.064
Uh... Marmaduke. Mama-what?


00:17:16.099 --> 00:17:20.436
Well, well. My little fireplug said
you were salivating on my girlfriend.


00:17:20.471 --> 00:17:24.157
No, no. I remember, somebody
walked by eating beef jerky.


00:17:24.224 --> 00:17:25.641
Let me explain something.


00:17:25.708 --> 00:17:29.144
This is my park,
and these are my rules.


00:17:29.212 --> 00:17:31.264
You look at my girlfriend
again, and you're dead.


00:17:31.331 --> 00:17:32.481
You come near her,
you're dead.


00:17:32.548 --> 00:17:34.233
You talk to her,
and you're...


00:17:34.300 --> 00:17:35.584
Dead.


00:17:35.652 --> 00:17:37.169
We're dead.
Yeah, we're dead!


00:17:37.888 --> 00:17:39.621
He ain't nothing, watch.


00:17:39.656 --> 00:17:41.373
Come on, you
wanna go? You wanna go?


00:17:41.441 --> 00:17:43.142
No! No! No, no, no.


00:17:43.210 --> 00:17:46.461
Didn't think so.
Welcome to the O.C., mutt.


00:17:46.529 --> 00:17:48.130
Yeah,
stand clear, Horsie.


00:17:49.299 --> 00:17:51.500
See you at the
party tonight, not!


00:17:53.203 --> 00:17:54.853
Can I open
my eyes now?


00:17:54.888 --> 00:17:56.989
Don't listen
to that guy.


00:17:57.056 --> 00:17:59.124
Maybe listen to the
part about staying away


00:17:59.192 --> 00:18:01.193
from his girlfriend
or he'll kill you.


00:18:01.261 --> 00:18:03.229
What party was he
talking about?


00:18:03.297 --> 00:18:07.500
Nothing, just a bunch of snobs scratching
themselves under the yacht club pier.


00:18:07.567 --> 00:18:09.735
We're having our
own party tonight.


00:18:09.803 --> 00:18:13.021
It's gonna be a classic O.C.
rager, you should totally come.


00:18:13.089 --> 00:18:15.224
Not sure if I can get out, but I'll try.


00:18:15.291 --> 00:18:16.975
Great, it's gonna be
a really good party!


00:18:17.043 --> 00:18:19.244
If you know what a party's like,
it's gonna be better than that.


00:18:19.312 --> 00:18:21.030
Tell them you know me!
You'll get right in.


00:18:21.098 --> 00:18:22.732
Thanks, Giuseppe!


00:18:24.234 --> 00:18:26.502
Good first day,
Marmaduke.


00:18:26.570 --> 00:18:30.155
You played it cool. And I think I
impressed a lot of dogs here today.


00:18:30.223 --> 00:18:31.907
Now, that is
a pretty good...


00:18:31.975 --> 00:18:34.009
Bee! Ahhh!


00:18:34.077 --> 00:18:36.345
A bee!
Get off of me now!


00:18:36.412 --> 00:18:38.731
Look out!
Phil, help me!


00:18:38.798 --> 00:18:41.500
Bark Organics dominates
the California market.


00:18:41.568 --> 00:18:43.369
With our product
recognition and quality,


00:18:43.437 --> 00:18:45.571
we're in a position
to crush the competition.


00:18:47.207 --> 00:18:50.209
So, Dorothy, why have I called
you all the way from Kansas?


00:18:50.277 --> 00:18:54.180
Why have I been through six
marketing directors in the last year?


00:18:54.247 --> 00:18:56.499
Because I want
Bark Organics


00:18:56.566 --> 00:18:58.300
on the shelves in every
PETCO in the country.


00:18:58.502 --> 00:19:01.370
Bee!
I can't see! Bee!


00:19:01.437 --> 00:19:03.289
I won't
let you down, sir.


00:19:04.141 --> 00:19:05.141
We'll see.
Watch out!


00:19:05.208 --> 00:19:06.842
Coming through!


00:19:06.927 --> 00:19:08.827
Sorry!
Are you okay?


00:19:08.895 --> 00:19:10.012
Was that your dog?


00:19:10.080 --> 00:19:11.614
I didn't get a good look.


00:19:11.681 --> 00:19:15.084
Yeah, I'm fine.
I'm fine!


00:19:15.152 --> 00:19:17.002
It takes a lot
more than that...


00:19:18.505 --> 00:19:20.655
Bee!
That dog!


00:19:20.723 --> 00:19:22.425
Phil, help!
Phil, get rid of him!


00:19:23.793 --> 00:19:25.978
Help me!
Why do bees hate me?


00:19:26.045 --> 00:19:28.113
What a gargantuan spaz!


00:19:28.181 --> 00:19:30.716
Yeah, but kind of funny.


00:19:32.352 --> 00:19:33.352
Hmm.


00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:40.609
I heard a vicious rumor that
you're, like, from Kansas?


00:19:40.677 --> 00:19:44.046
Yeah. Are those,
like, real dogs?


00:19:44.113 --> 00:19:46.114
The canine accessory
is so essential.


00:19:46.182 --> 00:19:48.033
We are not accessories.


00:19:48.101 --> 00:19:50.719
Hey, man,
in my country, I was a lawyer.


00:19:50.754 --> 00:19:53.706
I've been in this
purse so long, I can't feel my legs.


00:19:55.975 --> 00:19:57.677
Bodie is
so gorgeous!


00:19:59.095 --> 00:20:00.930
Did he just
look at me?


00:20:00.997 --> 00:20:02.682
As if!


00:20:02.749 --> 00:20:06.168
Yeah, you're probably right. He
probably wasn't looking at me.


00:20:07.804 --> 00:20:09.404
Hey, honey!


00:20:09.472 --> 00:20:12.424
Oh, my God!
Is that thing yours?


00:20:12.492 --> 00:20:14.259
No, it's somebody
else's dog. Not mine.


00:20:14.327 --> 00:20:16.528
Hey, Barb!
Who are your friends?


00:20:18.031 --> 00:20:20.382
Phil! That was not cool!


00:20:21.184 --> 00:20:22.351
Sorry, Barb.


00:20:24.087 --> 00:20:26.121
Right. Regional
market share first...


00:20:26.189 --> 00:20:27.623
Yeah, yeah.


00:20:27.691 --> 00:20:30.409
Come on, Phil, get off the
phone. Brian's going to bed.


00:20:30.477 --> 00:20:31.593
Night, Dad.


00:20:31.661 --> 00:20:32.928
Hey, Brian, wait up.


00:20:32.996 --> 00:20:35.914
Sounds good. We'll talk
tomorrow. Chill, Marmaduke.


00:20:35.982 --> 00:20:36.948
Great news!


00:20:37.016 --> 00:20:38.917
I ran into another
dad at the dog park,


00:20:38.985 --> 00:20:40.820
and guess what
he's in charge of?


00:20:42.222 --> 00:20:43.356
I signed you up!


00:20:43.423 --> 00:20:45.875
Oh. Soccer sounds...


00:20:45.942 --> 00:20:47.109
Great, right?


00:20:48.595 --> 00:20:50.179
Sure, yeah.


00:20:50.246 --> 00:20:51.464
Man, you're
gonna love it.


00:20:51.531 --> 00:20:54.216
Okay. Good night, Dad.


00:20:54.284 --> 00:20:55.800
Good night, buddy.


00:20:55.868 --> 00:20:58.970
Phil, he's not gonna love it. He's
gonna hate it, you knucklehead!


00:20:59.038 --> 00:21:00.655
Come on!


00:21:00.723 --> 00:21:03.141
I really miss
you guys, too.


00:21:03.209 --> 00:21:06.161
But I did see this
cute surfer kid today.


00:21:06.229 --> 00:21:08.680
You need anything, honey?


00:21:08.748 --> 00:21:11.416
A little privacy, and a
one-way ticket back to Kansas.


00:21:12.502 --> 00:21:13.702
Good night.


00:21:13.770 --> 00:21:16.121
Come on, Phil. It's like
you're not listening to them.


00:21:22.578 --> 00:21:26.098
# Lullaby, lullaby


00:21:26.165 --> 00:21:30.703
# All the humans
are sleeping #


00:21:32.155 --> 00:21:34.205
Ladies, please!


00:21:34.273 --> 00:21:36.558
Carlos, be quiet!


00:21:36.626 --> 00:21:38.861
Your eyes are
getting sleepy.


00:21:39.979 --> 00:21:41.880
So sleepy.


00:21:42.849 --> 00:21:45.534
Good night, Phil.


00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.792
# Hey, yo, when I wake up
moaning, yawning


00:21:52.859 --> 00:21:54.259
# I put up my hands


00:21:54.327 --> 00:21:55.661
# Thank the Lord
for what I got


00:21:55.729 --> 00:21:57.129
# and never stop my plans


00:21:57.196 --> 00:21:58.764
# Giving all for the goals


00:21:58.832 --> 00:22:00.165
# Got to keep it up,
never let my head drop


00:22:00.233 --> 00:22:01.867
# Make me a home on my own


00:22:01.934 --> 00:22:03.168
# Better make the bed rock #


00:22:04.621 --> 00:22:06.388
I'm a monster!


00:22:06.456 --> 00:22:07.740
I am a tiny monster.


00:22:07.807 --> 00:22:09.140
I'm doing the spin!


00:22:09.208 --> 00:22:11.660
This is an O.C. rager?


00:22:11.728 --> 00:22:13.412
You made it, great!


00:22:13.447 --> 00:22:15.281
Come watch Giuseppe
rip it up!


00:22:15.348 --> 00:22:18.700
Check this out!
One leg, one leg...


00:22:18.768 --> 00:22:20.168
Hey, Marmaduke!


00:22:20.236 --> 00:22:22.771
If you're hungry or thirsty,
the trash can's out back.


00:22:22.839 --> 00:22:24.256
And the toilet's in there.


00:22:24.324 --> 00:22:25.174
Cool, thanks!


00:22:26.376 --> 00:22:27.793
Did that cow just oink?


00:22:27.861 --> 00:22:31.680
Meet Mazie's cow.
The factory made a mistake.


00:22:31.748 --> 00:22:33.782
It's pretty ridiculous.


00:22:33.849 --> 00:22:36.585
Cow that oinks.
I think it's cool!


00:22:39.422 --> 00:22:41.907
New record!
Holler at your boy!


00:22:41.975 --> 00:22:43.709
Marmaduke, you're up!


00:22:43.776 --> 00:22:45.777
No, that's
cool. I'll just watch.


00:22:45.845 --> 00:22:49.831
Don't be a wiener dog! Just dance
along to the flashing arrows!


00:22:51.935 --> 00:22:54.570
I'd love to, but seriously,
guys, I've got four left paws.


00:22:54.605 --> 00:22:56.938
Duke!
Duke! Duke! Duke!


00:22:57.006 --> 00:23:00.041
All right, all right,
twist my paw. Duke! Duke!


00:23:00.109 --> 00:23:01.860
Atta boy!


00:23:06.182 --> 00:23:08.667
Okay, let's see.
This can't be that hard.


00:23:08.735 --> 00:23:11.453
Okay, let's see.
Right paw, white arrow.


00:23:11.488 --> 00:23:13.038
Left paw, blue arrow.


00:23:13.106 --> 00:23:14.339
No, no, left paw,
green arrow.


00:23:14.407 --> 00:23:15.991
There we go!


00:23:16.059 --> 00:23:18.510
On second thoughts, maybe
this wasn't such a good idea.


00:23:18.578 --> 00:23:20.295
Hang on,
give him a chance.


00:23:20.363 --> 00:23:21.363
You can do this, Marmy.


00:23:21.431 --> 00:23:23.081
Come on. Come on.
Come on, concentrate!


00:23:23.149 --> 00:23:24.483
Ease into it.


00:23:24.550 --> 00:23:25.734
Are we insured?


00:23:25.802 --> 00:23:27.845
No one puts Dukey
in a corner!


00:23:27.880 --> 00:23:29.888
The Duke's got
some moves!


00:23:29.955 --> 00:23:32.324
You ain't seen nothing yet!


00:23:33.893 --> 00:23:35.761
Time to get funky!


00:23:37.380 --> 00:23:38.680
He's better than me,
isn't he?


00:23:38.748 --> 00:23:39.781
In a way, yes.


00:23:42.152 --> 00:23:44.720
Three-sixty
on the big dog!


00:23:44.788 --> 00:23:45.921
Pinwheel time!


00:23:47.073 --> 00:23:48.724
Time to go old-school!


00:23:48.792 --> 00:23:50.575
Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:23:53.880 --> 00:23:56.915
I'm sorry. I'm really
sorry, guys. My bad.


00:23:56.983 --> 00:23:59.935
No sweat. I needed
to get a Wii, anyway.


00:24:00.002 --> 00:24:02.154
There goes Giuseppe's
entire social life.


00:24:02.221 --> 00:24:04.573
That was the only thing
I wasn't afraid of.


00:24:04.641 --> 00:24:08.326
You know, not that I'm not
having fun, because I totally am,


00:24:08.395 --> 00:24:11.446
what do you guys think about going to
the yacht club party, see what's up?


00:24:11.514 --> 00:24:12.914
Are you crazy?


00:24:12.982 --> 00:24:15.984
Or we could just go to the zoo,
and jump into the puma cage!


00:24:16.019 --> 00:24:18.169
Come on, it'll be fun!
Question.


00:24:18.238 --> 00:24:20.923
Are we gonna spend the rest of our
lives hiding underneath the porch


00:24:20.991 --> 00:24:22.458
with the little pups?


00:24:22.525 --> 00:24:25.210
Or are we gonna get out in
the yard with the big dogs?


00:24:25.278 --> 00:24:27.746
But we're not big dogs,
we're tiny dogs!


00:24:27.813 --> 00:24:29.748
That phrase was made
for dogs like you!


00:24:29.816 --> 00:24:32.051
You do realize
it's Bosco's party.


00:24:32.118 --> 00:24:36.054
Yeah, Bosco, Schmosco!
He's all bark, no bite.


00:24:36.122 --> 00:24:41.310
Okay. Some dogs just have
to learn the hard way.


00:24:41.377 --> 00:24:43.946
I smell rain, and I
did not dress for rain.


00:24:44.013 --> 00:24:45.697
I'm telling you guys,
without fur,


00:24:45.765 --> 00:24:47.332
it's like tiny bullets
from the sky.


00:24:50.086 --> 00:24:52.036
It's him!
Who is that?


00:24:52.104 --> 00:24:53.372
Chupadogra.


00:24:55.942 --> 00:24:57.626
Chupadogra?


00:24:59.128 --> 00:25:01.646
They say he was
the ultimate alpha dog.


00:25:01.714 --> 00:25:05.417
But then he went insane from
rabies and ate his owner.


00:25:05.484 --> 00:25:08.887
He also sleeps on a giant
pile of his victims' bones.


00:25:08.955 --> 00:25:11.674
Can we go now, before
I become an appetizer?


00:25:11.741 --> 00:25:13.875
Let's go.


00:25:13.943 --> 00:25:16.077
I can't believe
we survived Chupadogra!


00:25:16.145 --> 00:25:17.613
And now
he knows your scent.


00:25:17.680 --> 00:25:19.781
Why would you
say that?


00:25:19.849 --> 00:25:21.317
You sure you
wanna do this?


00:25:21.384 --> 00:25:23.068
Oh, yeah.
You bet I do.


00:25:23.136 --> 00:25:25.370
Guys, I'm telling you,
the tide is rising!


00:25:37.517 --> 00:25:39.718
Twenty-four,
come on, you can do it.


00:25:39.769 --> 00:25:41.136
Twenty-five!


00:25:41.204 --> 00:25:43.606
Man! Now, this party
is off the leash!


00:25:44.957 --> 00:25:46.408
What are they doing
to that cat?


00:25:47.560 --> 00:25:49.211
What pedigrees do best.


00:25:49.279 --> 00:25:50.462
Humiliate the innocent.


00:25:50.529 --> 00:25:53.198
Hey, wait, what are you
doing? Don't go over there!


00:25:53.266 --> 00:25:56.885
Come on, let's get
our bark on. Oh, oh...


00:25:56.953 --> 00:25:59.171
Oh, sorry.
I'll go this way.


00:26:00.773 --> 00:26:02.540
No problem. Sorry.


00:26:03.960 --> 00:26:05.744
This unfortunately
happens to me all the time.


00:26:06.312 --> 00:26:07.795
Me, too.


00:26:07.830 --> 00:26:10.182
Oh, brother!


00:26:12.168 --> 00:26:14.252
Great, we're getting
mad-dogged. Let's bail!


00:26:14.320 --> 00:26:17.573
Well, well, well. If it
isn't the dog and pony show.


00:26:17.641 --> 00:26:19.657
Did the circus give
you guys the day off?


00:26:19.725 --> 00:26:21.760
We're just leaving Bosco,
back off.


00:26:21.827 --> 00:26:25.180
Whoa, whoa, whoa! What's
the hurry? You just got here.


00:26:26.766 --> 00:26:29.368
You know, it's funny,
with ears like that


00:26:29.435 --> 00:26:31.069
I would have thought
you heard me tell you


00:26:31.136 --> 00:26:32.787
to stay away
from my girlfriend.


00:26:32.822 --> 00:26:34.489
He told him. You told
him, like, 12 times...


00:26:34.557 --> 00:26:36.892
Zip it!
Zipped!


00:26:36.959 --> 00:26:40.028
Being a pedigree means
you're exceptional.


00:26:40.096 --> 00:26:41.730
We're all bred
for a purpose


00:26:41.797 --> 00:26:45.167
and have gifts you could
never dream of having.


00:26:45.235 --> 00:26:48.053
Stuart's an expert tracker.


00:26:48.121 --> 00:26:49.872
Shasta is
a master sled dog.


00:26:51.407 --> 00:26:54.676
Ferdinand is fluent in six
languages, including gopher.


00:26:56.679 --> 00:27:00.782
And I'm the reigning
SoCal surf champ.


00:27:00.850 --> 00:27:03.518
Are you good
at anything? Huh?


00:27:04.020 --> 00:27:05.920
Um... Uh...


00:27:05.988 --> 00:27:07.055
Sit!


00:27:07.957 --> 00:27:10.559
You are
good at something!


00:27:14.330 --> 00:27:17.765
Lay down. Lay down!
That's it.


00:27:17.833 --> 00:27:19.451
Oh, no!
This is bad, isn't it?


00:27:19.518 --> 00:27:21.085
Yes, it's very bad.


00:27:24.273 --> 00:27:27.642
I don't care how freakishly
large you are, Donkey Boy.


00:27:27.710 --> 00:27:34.432
We all know that inside you're
just a scared little pup!


00:27:34.500 --> 00:27:36.000
Did I say you could
get up? No, no. Please!


00:27:36.068 --> 00:27:37.986
Did I say you could get up? I'm sorry!


00:27:38.054 --> 00:27:39.238
No mercy, boss.


00:27:39.305 --> 00:27:40.372
Put him in
a doggie bag!


00:27:40.440 --> 00:27:42.207
Fight! Fight! Fight!


00:27:42.274 --> 00:27:43.458
I don't
wanna fight you.


00:27:43.526 --> 00:27:44.576
Bosco, stop!


00:27:44.644 --> 00:27:47.345
Relax, baby! We're
just horsing around.


00:27:47.413 --> 00:27:49.815
No, you're not.
You're being a bully.


00:27:51.650 --> 00:27:55.337
I'm sorry, he gets this way when
he drinks too much drain-pipe water.


00:27:55.405 --> 00:27:57.939
He gets that way
because he's a jerk.


00:27:57.974 --> 00:27:59.558
You watch yourself, tomboy.


00:28:00.643 --> 00:28:02.644
Come on,
we're out of here.


00:28:05.548 --> 00:28:08.533
Come on, baby, are you gonna
spend time with them or with me?


00:28:11.254 --> 00:28:13.071
It's a party,
let's have fun!


00:28:14.857 --> 00:28:18.594
See you later, when there's not
any girls around to save you.


00:28:18.629 --> 00:28:19.577
Mutt.


00:28:28.571 --> 00:28:32.174
Bosco's right about everything.
I'm just a Gigantor freak.


00:28:32.241 --> 00:28:34.809
Wasn't bred for anything,
but getting in the way.


00:28:34.877 --> 00:28:37.061
You know, if I had a bone
for every time someone said,


00:28:37.129 --> 00:28:40.065
"Put a saddle on that thing!"
or, "How's the weather up there?"


00:28:40.133 --> 00:28:42.600
I'd be a bone-illionaire!


00:28:42.668 --> 00:28:46.638
Just once in my life, I'd
like to fit in, you know?


00:28:46.705 --> 00:28:50.759
Look, I know what it's
like to be an outsider.


00:28:50.827 --> 00:28:54.395
Okay? I was a rescue dog.
Nobody wanted me.


00:28:54.464 --> 00:28:57.699
But you're better than any of
those guys, and I can prove it.


00:28:57.767 --> 00:29:00.736
I can make you into
the dog you wanna be.


00:29:00.803 --> 00:29:04.055
Really? Why would
you do that for me?


00:29:04.123 --> 00:29:05.957
Because you're my friend.


00:29:08.043 --> 00:29:09.611
Wait, what time is it?


00:29:09.679 --> 00:29:11.830
Oh, man, Phil's gonna
get up soon. I got to go!


00:29:11.897 --> 00:29:13.665
I'll see you later!


00:29:16.852 --> 00:29:18.320
You're welcome.


00:29:32.451 --> 00:29:33.919
I just made it.


00:29:39.559 --> 00:29:42.494
I am beat.
I am so tired.


00:29:44.163 --> 00:29:45.797
I'm exhausted.


00:29:47.934 --> 00:29:49.901
Oh! Phil,
hit the snooze!


00:29:52.271 --> 00:29:53.338
Time for work,
big guy.


00:29:53.406 --> 00:29:55.506
Oh, Phil,
you're killing me.


00:29:56.742 --> 00:29:58.609
Winslow, Twombly.


00:29:58.677 --> 00:30:01.646
I need that new campaign and I need
it yesterday. So what do you got?


00:30:01.713 --> 00:30:03.765
Yeah. I got some
great ideas percolating,


00:30:03.833 --> 00:30:05.533
I just need a little
time to flesh them out.


00:30:05.601 --> 00:30:06.934
See, you got nothing.


00:30:07.002 --> 00:30:10.639
No, you can count on me.
It's gonna be a home run.


00:30:10.990 --> 00:30:11.689
It better be.


00:30:11.757 --> 00:30:12.957
Yeah, bye.


00:30:14.127 --> 00:30:15.427
I got nothing.


00:30:17.246 --> 00:30:20.181
Bee! Bee! Phil, get him!


00:30:20.216 --> 00:30:21.500
Marmaduke, relax!


00:30:21.567 --> 00:30:23.101
Phil, I hate bees!
Get back.


00:30:23.169 --> 00:30:25.203
Bee! Bee!
He's gonna sting us!


00:30:25.270 --> 00:30:29.525
He's gonna sting me and give me
rabies! Phil, Phil, get rid of him!


00:30:29.592 --> 00:30:31.492
Marmaduke, chill, relax.


00:30:31.728 --> 00:30:33.211
They're just surfers.


00:30:35.981 --> 00:30:37.449
Marmaduke,


00:30:38.785 --> 00:30:40.218
you're a genius!


00:30:40.286 --> 00:30:42.254
I am?


00:30:42.321 --> 00:30:44.305
A surf competition
for dogs?


00:30:44.373 --> 00:30:47.292
Picture this. Man's best
friend surfing towards shore,


00:30:47.360 --> 00:30:49.594
throngs of owners
cheering them on.


00:30:49.662 --> 00:30:52.247
How's that gonna sell organic
dog food to the heartland?


00:30:52.315 --> 00:30:53.815
Eleven o'clock, Phil.


00:30:53.883 --> 00:30:57.219
Listen, if you wanna sell to
the Midwest, I'll tell you how.


00:30:57.287 --> 00:30:58.954
Be true to
who you are.


00:30:59.022 --> 00:31:02.457
Bark Organics was made in
Southern California, embrace that.


00:31:02.525 --> 00:31:04.927
Bring the iconic spirit
of the West Coast


00:31:04.994 --> 00:31:07.129
to every dog owner
across the country.


00:31:07.196 --> 00:31:09.197
I don't know.


00:31:09.265 --> 00:31:12.100
I hired you to create an
identity for this company


00:31:12.168 --> 00:31:14.403
and you're telling me
to be myself?


00:31:14.470 --> 00:31:16.371
You know, we only have
one shot with PETCO.


00:31:16.439 --> 00:31:17.689
I know.


00:31:19.392 --> 00:31:21.659
But you got to
trust me on this.


00:31:23.363 --> 00:31:24.997
All right.


00:31:25.064 --> 00:31:27.532
One shot.
Make it happen.


00:31:28.785 --> 00:31:30.519
Yes!


00:31:30.586 --> 00:31:33.021
Okay, mutt-makeover
begins now.


00:31:33.089 --> 00:31:34.039
First things first.


00:31:34.106 --> 00:31:36.925
All right,
I'm all ears, literally.


00:31:36.993 --> 00:31:38.210
Pig Cow is yours.


00:31:38.277 --> 00:31:41.579
Check, Pig Cow's mine. Why?


00:31:41.647 --> 00:31:43.548
He's a real confidence
booster. Of course he is.


00:31:43.615 --> 00:31:45.183
You just chew on him
when you get nervous.


00:31:45.251 --> 00:31:46.884
Noted and filed.


00:31:46.952 --> 00:31:48.303
Next up,
let's smell that breath.


00:31:49.889 --> 00:31:51.373
Whoa!


00:31:51.440 --> 00:31:53.692
Oh, buddy!


00:31:53.759 --> 00:31:55.193
Really, that bad?


00:31:55.261 --> 00:31:58.763
That needs work. Okay, pedigrees
have dental hygienists, all right?


00:31:58.831 --> 00:32:00.765
So garbage breath
is not gonna cut it.


00:32:00.833 --> 00:32:03.518
Stay out of trash cans and
eat more mint-based items.


00:32:03.553 --> 00:32:05.470
Okay, less trash,
more mint.


00:32:05.538 --> 00:32:06.905
And stand up proud.


00:32:06.972 --> 00:32:09.775
Your ancestors sat
at the foot of kings, man.


00:32:09.810 --> 00:32:10.725
Yeah.


00:32:10.793 --> 00:32:12.728
Let's put the "Great"
back in "Dane" here.


00:32:12.795 --> 00:32:16.030
Yeah, like this?
Um...


00:32:16.098 --> 00:32:18.750
You know, just maybe keep your
ears up, too, while we're at it.


00:32:18.817 --> 00:32:21.786
Ears up. Like this?


00:32:21.854 --> 00:32:23.922
Yeah, that looks fine.


00:32:24.857 --> 00:32:26.224
Just out of curiosity,


00:32:26.292 --> 00:32:30.111
do you think any of this
stuff would work with girls?


00:32:30.179 --> 00:32:33.982
Did you
have anyone in mind?


00:32:34.050 --> 00:32:36.484
Not specifically, just
thinking out loud here.


00:32:38.070 --> 00:32:40.271
Oh!


00:32:40.339 --> 00:32:43.808
Right, right, okay. No
one specific. That's good.


00:32:46.062 --> 00:32:47.871
Okay...


00:32:47.906 --> 00:32:49.681
Listen up, Barkanova.


00:32:49.748 --> 00:32:54.202
If it were me, I'd want him
to take me to the junkyard.


00:32:54.270 --> 00:32:56.554
It's really
romantic there at night.


00:32:56.622 --> 00:32:59.440
There'd be a blanket
with some treats spread out,


00:32:59.508 --> 00:33:02.861
music from an old car
radio playing softly.


00:33:02.928 --> 00:33:06.364
Yeah, and lots of great
old stuff to pee on, right?


00:33:06.431 --> 00:33:08.884
Oh! You've got
so much to learn.


00:33:08.951 --> 00:33:12.754
Here's the deal.
Girls want romance.


00:33:12.821 --> 00:33:14.205
You know? Mystery.


00:33:14.973 --> 00:33:16.207
Wow.


00:33:16.642 --> 00:33:18.376
What?


00:33:18.443 --> 00:33:22.046
You know, I never really noticed
before, but you have really pretty...


00:33:23.565 --> 00:33:24.566
Fire truck!


00:33:24.633 --> 00:33:25.884
Hey, buddy,
we're talking here.


00:33:25.952 --> 00:33:27.619
Fire truck!
Heel!


00:33:27.687 --> 00:33:29.771
Oh, sorry.
Where were we?


00:33:29.839 --> 00:33:32.240
Uh... You said I
have really pretty...


00:33:32.308 --> 00:33:33.492
Got to go, buddy.
Work to do.


00:33:33.559 --> 00:33:35.627
No! Wait, Phil,
no, not now!


00:33:35.695 --> 00:33:36.794
Hey, where are you going?


00:33:36.862 --> 00:33:38.112
Phil, I need this.


00:33:38.180 --> 00:33:39.948
Come on. Let's go.
"Really pretty" what?


00:33:40.015 --> 00:33:41.182
What?


00:33:45.554 --> 00:33:47.105
Carlos, let
me ask you something.


00:33:47.172 --> 00:33:48.973
Is my breath
really that bad?


00:33:49.041 --> 00:33:50.541
A tube of toothpaste is a good start,


00:33:50.609 --> 00:33:53.195
but you're gonna
need more than that.


00:33:53.262 --> 00:33:54.829
Dude, watch it!


00:33:54.897 --> 00:33:56.430
Just gave myself
a tongue-bath.


00:33:56.498 --> 00:33:57.649
Sorry.


00:33:59.018 --> 00:34:00.151
How's my breath now?


00:34:01.621 --> 00:34:04.022
Refreshingly minty.


00:34:04.190 --> 00:34:06.958
Who am I kidding? Minty
breath, better posture.


00:34:07.026 --> 00:34:08.860
This stuff's
never gonna work.


00:34:08.927 --> 00:34:12.914
These guys have real skills.
I could never speak gopher.


00:34:12.981 --> 00:34:14.449
Why would you want
to talk to gophers?


00:34:14.516 --> 00:34:16.134
Forget it.


00:34:16.202 --> 00:34:18.069
Breaking into
new cliques is tough


00:34:18.137 --> 00:34:21.589
and breaking into bird cages
is even tougher.


00:34:21.657 --> 00:34:22.974
I just don't get it.


00:34:23.042 --> 00:34:25.376
I'm a dog and you're a
cat, we get along great.


00:34:25.444 --> 00:34:27.578
That's because
you're my hermano.


00:34:27.646 --> 00:34:30.114
If we weren't related, I'd
scratch both your eyes out!


00:34:32.985 --> 00:34:34.452
Don't make me laugh.


00:34:34.520 --> 00:34:35.953
You could never take me.


00:34:36.021 --> 00:34:39.040
I'd cream your
furry little butt...


00:34:39.808 --> 00:34:42.244
Carlos, you're a genius.


00:34:43.412 --> 00:34:45.413
What is he doing?


00:34:46.499 --> 00:34:49.634
Say, does anybody
smell that?


00:34:49.702 --> 00:34:53.654
I smell a cat
and I hate cats.


00:34:53.722 --> 00:34:56.091
Cat! There's
no cat here.


00:34:56.158 --> 00:34:59.394
I said,
"I smell a cat."


00:35:02.047 --> 00:35:03.848
Where am I? Hey boss, there is a cat!


00:35:03.916 --> 00:35:07.101
No, no, no.
This one's mine, fellas.


00:35:07.169 --> 00:35:10.371
Is this a dog park?
I must be horribly lost.


00:35:10.439 --> 00:35:12.573
Oh, yeah,
you must be lost, cat,


00:35:12.641 --> 00:35:14.976
because this park
is for dogs only.


00:35:15.094 --> 00:35:16.494
I got the tail!


00:35:16.562 --> 00:35:17.979
You said there'd
only be a few dogs.


00:35:18.047 --> 00:35:19.680
It's a dog park. What
do you want me to do?


00:35:19.748 --> 00:35:21.416
The sun's out,
it's crowded today.


00:35:21.484 --> 00:35:23.584
This is gonna
cost you, big time!


00:35:23.652 --> 00:35:25.020
Fight! Fight!


00:35:25.087 --> 00:35:26.938
Whoa!
What a crowd!


00:35:27.005 --> 00:35:28.122
Who let the dogs out?


00:35:28.190 --> 00:35:29.657
This doesn't
look good!


00:35:29.725 --> 00:35:31.325
Please don't
hurt me, Mister.


00:35:31.393 --> 00:35:33.694
I'm just a poor,
incredibly attractive,


00:35:33.762 --> 00:35:36.665
ultra-intelligent cat,
who has lost his way.


00:35:36.732 --> 00:35:41.236
You're gonna need all nine lives
after this beat-down, pussycat.


00:35:41.304 --> 00:35:45.507
You are the biggest, baddest
dog I have ever seen in my life.


00:35:45.575 --> 00:35:48.076
You also seem very
cool and confident.


00:35:48.143 --> 00:35:49.277
You're right
about all of that,


00:35:49.345 --> 00:35:51.746
you little
Fancy-Feast-eating freak!


00:35:51.813 --> 00:35:53.598
Please! Spare my life!


00:35:53.666 --> 00:35:55.333
Spare this.


00:35:55.400 --> 00:35:58.103
Come on, sell it, man.
Sell it.


00:35:58.138 --> 00:36:00.154
Really? Okay.


00:36:00.222 --> 00:36:02.406
Left jab, left jab,
work the body.


00:36:03.993 --> 00:36:06.461
Get back here, you
good-for-nothing little fur-ball!


00:36:06.529 --> 00:36:07.846
I only
weigh six pounds.


00:36:07.913 --> 00:36:09.898
This officially
hurts now. Stop!


00:36:09.966 --> 00:36:12.701
No, no, keep going, keep
going. I think it's working.


00:36:12.768 --> 00:36:14.802
Maybe we can find
a happy medium?


00:36:15.020 --> 00:36:16.270
Yeah, yeah, yeah.


00:36:16.338 --> 00:36:18.039
Hey, everybody,
watch this!


00:36:18.157 --> 00:36:20.942
No, no, no!
Whoa, whoa, whoa!


00:36:21.010 --> 00:36:22.126
Dizzy!


00:36:27.249 --> 00:36:28.649
Hairball.


00:36:28.718 --> 00:36:31.686
What's the matter, Bigglesworth?
Dog got your tongue?


00:36:31.754 --> 00:36:33.454
Yeah, whatever, man.


00:36:34.506 --> 00:36:36.173
Hope you got
what you wanted.


00:36:38.377 --> 00:36:41.245
That was hilarious, Marmadonk!


00:36:41.313 --> 00:36:43.447
Yeah, you're not
as good as Bosco,


00:36:43.516 --> 00:36:45.583
but you took that
fleabag to school!


00:36:45.651 --> 00:36:49.470
Oh, please, it was a cat.
It's not like he killed it.


00:36:49.538 --> 00:36:51.572
You've got a keen
sense of smell.


00:36:51.640 --> 00:36:55.209
Oh. Well, thanks.
It must be the large nostrils.


00:36:55.277 --> 00:36:58.913
I have to go, but maybe
I'll see you around.


00:36:59.398 --> 00:37:01.066
Cool! I'd like that.


00:37:01.133 --> 00:37:04.052
Jezebel,
let's go. Now!


00:37:05.387 --> 00:37:07.822
You know, I have a
pretty good nose myself


00:37:07.889 --> 00:37:11.258
and when I'm around you
I smell potential,


00:37:11.326 --> 00:37:12.927
with a hint of
something minty.


00:37:12.995 --> 00:37:14.796
I like it.
Let's go!


00:37:17.733 --> 00:37:19.484
It worked!
She talked to me!


00:37:19.552 --> 00:37:22.670
What are you doing? That's
not what we talked about!


00:37:22.738 --> 00:37:25.222
Who cares?
She liked my minty breath!


00:37:29.145 --> 00:37:33.414
Welcome to the First Annual Bark
Organics Dog Surfing Competition.


00:37:33.482 --> 00:37:37.368
Dogs and owners, make your
way to the shore. Cowabarka!


00:37:49.314 --> 00:37:51.582
Hey, I know you.
You go to Marshall, right?


00:37:52.384 --> 00:37:53.585
The new girl.


00:37:54.203 --> 00:37:55.369
That's me.


00:37:56.505 --> 00:37:58.339
You ever not
on that thing?


00:38:00.392 --> 00:38:01.593
You ever not
on that thing?


00:38:03.078 --> 00:38:04.078
I'm Bodie.


00:38:04.146 --> 00:38:05.513
I know. I mean...


00:38:06.181 --> 00:38:07.415
Yeah, I'm Barbara.


00:38:08.100 --> 00:38:10.468
Is that your dog?


00:38:10.535 --> 00:38:12.419
No, no, no.
That's my dad's dog.


00:38:12.487 --> 00:38:14.155
Huh. That's too bad.


00:38:14.223 --> 00:38:16.324
He's way better than
those lame purse dogs.


00:38:16.391 --> 00:38:19.644
Well, I did kind of adopt him
as my own, though.


00:38:19.712 --> 00:38:21.646
The dog, not my dad.


00:38:21.714 --> 00:38:24.349
Yeah, Marmaduke and I
are super close.


00:38:27.069 --> 00:38:30.271
My friend's having a party
next weekend. You should come.


00:38:30.339 --> 00:38:31.856
Sure, I'd love to.


00:38:33.792 --> 00:38:36.260
Competition's starting.
Beat it, Hasselhoff.


00:38:37.412 --> 00:38:39.446
Dad,
what are you doing?


00:38:39.514 --> 00:38:42.049
You're way too young, and I'm way
too busy to talk about this right now.


00:38:43.619 --> 00:38:45.670
And, just put
some clothes on.


00:38:45.738 --> 00:38:47.371
Can I get you
anything, Deb?


00:38:51.410 --> 00:38:52.910
He's cute!


00:38:55.447 --> 00:38:58.248
Hey, Marmaduke,
can you keep a secret?


00:38:59.117 --> 00:39:00.601
Probably.


00:39:01.904 --> 00:39:05.940
I've been telling Dad
I'm going to soccer practice,


00:39:06.008 --> 00:39:08.776
but I've actually been
hanging out at the skate park.


00:39:08.844 --> 00:39:10.778
I think that
sounds cool, Brian.


00:39:10.846 --> 00:39:12.647
But you got to
tell your dad.


00:39:12.714 --> 00:39:15.783
I don't even
like soccer.


00:39:15.851 --> 00:39:18.686
I guess I just don't know
how to tell him the truth.


00:39:18.753 --> 00:39:21.789
I hear you, bro,
but just hang in there.


00:39:22.525 --> 00:39:25.342
I wish you could talk.


00:39:25.410 --> 00:39:28.412
And I wish you could
understand me.


00:39:28.714 --> 00:39:30.265
Come on, Marmaduke!


00:39:30.332 --> 00:39:32.383
Hey, Brian, you okay?
Yeah.


00:39:32.451 --> 00:39:35.403
What do you say we kick
that ball around later?


00:39:35.471 --> 00:39:37.421
No, I'm good.


00:39:37.489 --> 00:39:38.672
Come on, buddy.
Wait! Phil! Phil!


00:39:38.740 --> 00:39:42.076
Hold on, Phil. Brian's
got something to tell you.


00:39:45.297 --> 00:39:49.984
It is a beautiful day here in
Southern California for dog surfing.


00:39:50.052 --> 00:39:53.855
Please, put your paws together
for our canine competitors!


00:39:53.922 --> 00:39:56.674
Aha! And here's our marketing
director, Phil Winslow.


00:39:56.741 --> 00:39:59.843
Phil, this is David King,
Jessica Colestat from PETCO.


00:39:59.911 --> 00:40:01.462
Pleased to meet you.


00:40:01.530 --> 00:40:04.732
I hope you're ready for a
mind-blowing canine surf experience.


00:40:04.800 --> 00:40:08.035
Wow! Can't wait to see
this big guy out on the waves!


00:40:08.103 --> 00:40:09.470
No, no, no.


00:40:09.538 --> 00:40:12.023
Phil and Marmaduke are one
month removed from Kansas.


00:40:12.091 --> 00:40:13.758
I don't think they're ready to hang 10.


00:40:13.826 --> 00:40:16.076
Well, that's too bad. That
would've been hysterical.


00:40:16.145 --> 00:40:17.845
Yeah!


00:40:17.846 --> 00:40:22.016
No, you're right!
That would be hysterical! Phil?


00:40:22.083 --> 00:40:25.086
Phil, come on, they're
just kidding. Say no!


00:40:26.722 --> 00:40:28.556
Marmaduke's dying
to hang 20.


00:40:28.624 --> 00:40:29.824
Dying to.


00:40:29.891 --> 00:40:31.809
Oh! We're dead!


00:40:31.877 --> 00:40:33.027
No, no, no. Phil, no!


00:40:33.095 --> 00:40:34.112
Let's go, buddy.


00:40:34.179 --> 00:40:35.613
Come on.
It's just water.


00:40:35.680 --> 00:40:37.648
No. Way too big and
too wet! Cold, cold!


00:40:37.716 --> 00:40:40.735
That's my competition?
This ought to be fun.


00:40:40.803 --> 00:40:41.970
Freezing, freezing!


00:40:42.037 --> 00:40:43.838
No! Marmaduke!
Cold, cold!


00:40:43.905 --> 00:40:45.940
Come on,
get back here. Heel!


00:40:47.459 --> 00:40:49.476
Happy thoughts,
happy thoughts.


00:40:49.544 --> 00:40:52.513
I'm running through a meadow.
I'm peeing on everything.


00:40:52.580 --> 00:40:54.782
You don't stand
a chance, Shamu.


00:40:54.850 --> 00:40:55.916
I own these waves.


00:40:55.984 --> 00:40:57.952
Good luck to you, too.


00:40:58.020 --> 00:41:00.939
It's okay, Marmaduke.
Nothing bad's gonna happen.


00:41:01.006 --> 00:41:04.508
Something bad's gonna happen,
Phil. Payback's gonna hurt.


00:41:04.576 --> 00:41:05.926
Okay, stay.
It's okay.


00:41:05.995 --> 00:41:08.062
Ladies and gentlemen, take
a look, on the horizon,


00:41:08.130 --> 00:41:10.898
a massive,
rogue wave approaches!


00:41:10.966 --> 00:41:13.600
You got to be kidding!


00:41:13.668 --> 00:41:15.319
Time to dazzle.
It's all you, buddy.


00:41:15.387 --> 00:41:17.572
Phil! No, no, what are
you doing? Phil, help me.


00:41:17.607 --> 00:41:18.973
Phil, no!
Good luck!


00:41:19.040 --> 00:41:21.759
Somebody get me off this
thing! What am I doing?


00:41:21.826 --> 00:41:23.261
Out of my way, poser! Look out!


00:41:23.328 --> 00:41:24.595
I've got
the right of way!


00:41:24.663 --> 00:41:25.730
Oh, boy!


00:41:25.797 --> 00:41:27.582
Look out!
Phil, help me!


00:41:27.650 --> 00:41:29.701
Look at this!
It's Marmaduke!


00:41:29.768 --> 00:41:32.086
Look at the perfect position
here, Marmaduke in the barrel.


00:41:32.154 --> 00:41:33.404
Yeah!


00:41:33.471 --> 00:41:37.308
Get me off this thing!
Help! Marmy don't surf!


00:41:37.376 --> 00:41:39.911
He doesn't look like
he's gonna make it.


00:41:39.978 --> 00:41:41.212
Where is he?


00:41:41.280 --> 00:41:42.564
I don't know.


00:41:44.016 --> 00:41:45.699
Oh, man,
I'm gonna die!


00:41:45.767 --> 00:41:47.935
No, you're not.
Get a hold of yourself!


00:41:48.003 --> 00:41:50.170
Grip it and rip it!


00:41:50.205 --> 00:41:51.622
Geronimo!


00:41:54.126 --> 00:41:56.460
There he is!


00:41:58.263 --> 00:42:00.814
Take a look at this!
He throws a big air!


00:42:00.882 --> 00:42:02.667
What a crazy dog!


00:42:03.686 --> 00:42:06.554
Look out! Look out!


00:42:07.956 --> 00:42:12.343
And the Duke shreds!
This dog rules! Marmaduke!


00:42:12.478 --> 00:42:14.478
You did it, buddy!
Oh! Get me out of here!


00:42:14.546 --> 00:42:16.364
That's my dog! Get this seaweed off me!


00:42:16.432 --> 00:42:18.149
It burns! It burns!


00:42:18.216 --> 00:42:19.751
Debbie, help!


00:42:20.735 --> 00:42:21.569
Yeah!


00:42:21.636 --> 00:42:23.320
That was awesome!
Really?


00:42:23.388 --> 00:42:25.389
That was off the hook! The
Duke has arrived, y'all!


00:42:25.457 --> 00:42:26.491
It was?


00:42:26.558 --> 00:42:28.092
You totally
shredded, dude!


00:42:28.159 --> 00:42:28.993
I shredded?


00:42:29.061 --> 00:42:30.661
That was way better
than Bosco, dude!


00:42:30.729 --> 00:42:32.679
Marmaduke shreds!


00:42:32.747 --> 00:42:37.651
All right, here it is.
The overall surf champion...


00:42:37.719 --> 00:42:40.988
You think it was funny dropping in
on my wave like that, Marma-puke?


00:42:41.056 --> 00:42:42.957
I didn't do
anything, Bosco!


00:42:43.025 --> 00:42:45.359
Let it go,
it was an accident.


00:42:45.427 --> 00:42:47.211
And the trophy
goes to...


00:42:47.278 --> 00:42:48.229
This better be me.


00:42:48.296 --> 00:42:50.681
Whoa! We have an upset.


00:42:50.749 --> 00:42:54.151
The trophy goes to Phil
Winslow and Marmaduke!


00:42:55.353 --> 00:42:56.504
What?


00:42:56.572 --> 00:42:57.822
Phil, did we really win?


00:42:57.889 --> 00:43:00.107
I'm gonna tear
you apart, mutt.


00:43:00.142 --> 00:43:01.192
I didn't do anything!


00:43:01.260 --> 00:43:02.743
Somebody put a leash
on this dog!


00:43:02.778 --> 00:43:03.978
Marmaduke!


00:43:04.045 --> 00:43:05.780
Help!


00:43:06.865 --> 00:43:08.616
Get back here, mutt!


00:43:09.284 --> 00:43:11.135
Whoa, whoa!


00:43:11.202 --> 00:43:12.737
Get back here,
you poser!


00:43:12.804 --> 00:43:15.373
I don't even
like surfing!


00:43:15.440 --> 00:43:17.174
Stop running,
you coward.


00:43:17.242 --> 00:43:20.194
I'm gonna make you pay.
I am gonna make you pay!


00:43:21.312 --> 00:43:23.380
Come on, Duke,
you can take him.


00:43:23.448 --> 00:43:26.016
This ends right here,
right now.


00:43:26.084 --> 00:43:29.420
You know what? You're right,
Bosco. This does end here.


00:43:31.590 --> 00:43:33.424
Ow! My leg's cramping!
Ow! Ow!


00:43:33.492 --> 00:43:35.142
Time out, time out!


00:43:35.144 --> 00:43:36.394
No, bad dog!


00:43:37.412 --> 00:43:38.695
Heel.


00:43:39.731 --> 00:43:41.365
I'm so sorry
about this.


00:43:43.585 --> 00:43:46.220
Get your dog under
control, you understand?


00:43:48.273 --> 00:43:50.942
Come on, folks, I'm so
sorry. Come on. Come this way.


00:44:00.068 --> 00:44:04.204
Hey, what's the new surf
champ doing out here all alone?


00:44:04.272 --> 00:44:08.776
Hey. I'm just kind of here,
taking a break from the old family.


00:44:08.844 --> 00:44:11.996
Well, I guess some people just
can't handle it when you're top dog.


00:44:12.064 --> 00:44:13.214
Really?


00:44:15.734 --> 00:44:18.502
It's getting
a little cold out.


00:44:18.570 --> 00:44:20.688
Wait, what about Bosco?


00:44:20.755 --> 00:44:21.788
Forget about him.


00:44:21.856 --> 00:44:23.524
There's a new dog in town.


00:44:23.592 --> 00:44:25.860
And his name
is Marmaduke.


00:44:26.428 --> 00:44:28.396
Hey, that's my name!


00:44:30.031 --> 00:44:32.700
That's my name!
Marmaduke!


00:44:32.767 --> 00:44:34.835
Say it loud,
say it proud!


00:44:36.405 --> 00:44:39.206
# The moon was shining
on the lake at night


00:44:39.274 --> 00:44:43.377
# The Slayer T-shirt
fit the scene just right


00:44:43.445 --> 00:44:48.498
# Smeared mascara, I looked
into your eyes I saw a light #


00:44:49.751 --> 00:44:51.735
Fire truck!


00:44:51.803 --> 00:44:53.871
Fire truck!
Fire truck!


00:44:58.026 --> 00:44:59.594
Hi! Phil Winslow.


00:44:59.661 --> 00:45:02.162
Anton, master of
the Top Dog method.


00:45:02.230 --> 00:45:04.982
I'm supposed to listen
to a guy named Anton?


00:45:11.290 --> 00:45:13.775
Top dog him, Phil.
Top dog him.


00:45:17.662 --> 00:45:19.396
Marmaduke!


00:45:19.464 --> 00:45:20.664
Guys, what's going on?
Let's go.


00:45:20.732 --> 00:45:22.532
What are you doing?
Out of the car!


00:45:22.600 --> 00:45:23.600
Let's go.


00:45:25.554 --> 00:45:27.054
Oh...


00:45:30.842 --> 00:45:33.661
Pump your fists triumphantly,
and say it to the world,


00:45:33.728 --> 00:45:35.579
"I'm top dog!"
Rubber bone!


00:45:35.647 --> 00:45:36.881
I'm top dog!


00:45:36.949 --> 00:45:37.832
Bone! Give me!


00:45:46.975 --> 00:45:49.227
I thought
you said he'd be here.


00:45:49.294 --> 00:45:51.361
He said he might stop by
after the pedigree party,


00:45:51.429 --> 00:45:53.697
but he didn't
promise anything.


00:46:06.860 --> 00:46:08.510
How much farther?


00:46:08.578 --> 00:46:11.680
Just keep coming. Keep
coming, we're almost there.


00:46:13.783 --> 00:46:15.518
Where are we?


00:46:15.585 --> 00:46:17.620
It's a surprise. Ready?


00:46:17.655 --> 00:46:19.655
Hit it, boys!


00:46:21.207 --> 00:46:22.474
Wow!


00:46:27.730 --> 00:46:29.965
It's pretty cool,
isn't it?


00:46:33.353 --> 00:46:34.937
It's beautiful!


00:46:37.140 --> 00:46:39.008
Wait, wait, wait.
There's more.


00:46:39.075 --> 00:46:41.594
Crank it, DJ Thunder!


00:46:46.649 --> 00:46:49.185
I can't believe I'm
really here with you.


00:46:49.253 --> 00:46:52.437
Of course you are, silly!
You're the alpha dog.


00:46:52.505 --> 00:46:54.357
Okay, well,
I hope you're hungry.


00:46:54.424 --> 00:46:57.442
Wow! You really pulled
out all the stops!


00:46:57.510 --> 00:47:00.179
It's just a little
something I whipped up.


00:47:00.214 --> 00:47:02.398
How about a peanut
butter appetizer?


00:47:02.465 --> 00:47:04.283
My favorite!


00:47:04.350 --> 00:47:07.453
Really? I was worried you
might be allergic to it.


00:47:07.521 --> 00:47:09.121
I almost got
almond butter.


00:47:10.324 --> 00:47:13.192
It's so romantic!


00:47:13.260 --> 00:47:16.895
I couldn't think of another
girl I'd rather share it with.


00:47:16.964 --> 00:47:19.364
It's so creative, too.


00:47:19.432 --> 00:47:22.684
Tell me, how did you
ever think of this?


00:47:22.752 --> 00:47:24.803
It's just
the kind of guy I am.


00:47:24.871 --> 00:47:27.957
I'm a Great Dane. We
sat at the foot of kings!


00:47:29.926 --> 00:47:32.994
Listen, I just wanted
to say something.


00:47:33.062 --> 00:47:33.813
I wanted to say...


00:47:35.048 --> 00:47:36.849
My bad.
I slipped off the seat.


00:47:36.916 --> 00:47:40.135
That's okay, Thunder.
He's so funny.


00:47:40.187 --> 00:47:41.920
I wanted to say


00:47:41.988 --> 00:47:44.790
hanging out with you
these last few weeks,


00:47:44.858 --> 00:47:47.593
which in dog years
feels like months,


00:47:47.661 --> 00:47:51.564
it's like the first time in my
life I feel like I really belong.


00:47:51.698 --> 00:47:54.600
Yeah! I'm having
a great time, too.


00:48:10.250 --> 00:48:11.284
Look at him.


00:48:11.351 --> 00:48:13.869
Land shrimps at
his beck and call.


00:48:13.936 --> 00:48:15.036
That's it.


00:48:15.104 --> 00:48:17.306
No, Mazie!
Stay, please.


00:48:20.960 --> 00:48:22.561
Sit!
Yes, ma'am.


00:48:22.628 --> 00:48:23.930
Yes, ma'am.


00:48:25.782 --> 00:48:27.516
Hey, Mazie!
What's up?


00:48:27.584 --> 00:48:31.103
You don't give a steaming pile about
us anymore, so cut the act, all right?


00:48:31.170 --> 00:48:33.155
We took you in.
We were your friends.


00:48:33.222 --> 00:48:35.941
And you just sit over here
and act like we're dirt.


00:48:36.009 --> 00:48:38.143
What'd they put in your
kibble this morning?


00:48:38.211 --> 00:48:40.029
You took her
on my dream date.


00:48:40.097 --> 00:48:43.098
Dream date? What is she talking about?


00:48:43.166 --> 00:48:45.784
How do you think
that makes me feel?


00:48:47.587 --> 00:48:50.122
Bitter, party of one?


00:48:53.927 --> 00:48:55.327
What's the big deal?


00:48:55.395 --> 00:48:57.012
We were just
spit-balling ideas.


00:48:57.080 --> 00:48:59.097
You'd think she'd be
thrilled I used one.


00:48:59.165 --> 00:49:00.266
You don't get it,
do you?


00:49:00.333 --> 00:49:03.085
She gave you Pig Cow,
she likes you.


00:49:03.153 --> 00:49:05.221
At least, she did until
you turned your back on us


00:49:05.388 --> 00:49:07.889
and became a big
phony-baloney sell-out.


00:49:07.924 --> 00:49:09.475
Word.


00:49:09.543 --> 00:49:11.109
That's really cute
and everything,


00:49:11.177 --> 00:49:12.511
but I already
have a girlfriend.


00:49:12.579 --> 00:49:14.613
A pedigree girlfriend.


00:49:14.681 --> 00:49:16.531
So, that's it?


00:49:17.834 --> 00:49:18.717
Yeah.


00:49:19.953 --> 00:49:22.371
I don't hang out
with mutts anymore.


00:49:24.341 --> 00:49:25.341
Ouch!


00:49:28.478 --> 00:49:31.146
You're lucky
I had a favor to call in.


00:49:31.214 --> 00:49:33.064
PETCO's gonna give us
another chance.


00:49:33.132 --> 00:49:35.267
But they wanna see
a fully realized campaign


00:49:35.335 --> 00:49:37.135
before they'll
cross-promote the roll-out.


00:49:37.203 --> 00:49:39.288
No problem, I'll start
working on that immediately.


00:49:39.356 --> 00:49:41.223
You'll start
working on it?


00:49:41.291 --> 00:49:44.260
Little late for you to be
going solo, there, Buckeye.


00:49:44.327 --> 00:49:46.762
I want you on my boat this
weekend, we'll work together.


00:49:46.829 --> 00:49:48.664
This weekend, I can't. You have to.


00:49:48.731 --> 00:49:51.067
I need to spend some
quality time with my family.


00:49:51.134 --> 00:49:52.168
Tough.


00:49:52.235 --> 00:49:53.635
I promised my wife.


00:49:55.138 --> 00:49:57.973
All right, bring the family along.
They can relax while we work.


00:49:58.041 --> 00:50:00.109
Okay, that'll be perfect.


00:50:00.177 --> 00:50:01.510
Excellent.


00:50:03.480 --> 00:50:05.081
Now, this is
sort of embarrassing,


00:50:05.148 --> 00:50:07.015
but there are no dogs
allowed on the boat.


00:50:07.934 --> 00:50:09.584
It's my wife's rule.


00:50:09.586 --> 00:50:11.220
Quite frankly,


00:50:12.222 --> 00:50:15.023
I think she's jealous.


00:50:15.091 --> 00:50:16.858
Okay, we got the
life jacket, towels,


00:50:16.927 --> 00:50:18.978
bathing suits,
sunglasses, sunscreen.


00:50:19.045 --> 00:50:20.479
Brian's got his fins.


00:50:20.546 --> 00:50:21.813
You're taking
the laptop?


00:50:21.881 --> 00:50:24.649
You know,
just in case.


00:50:24.717 --> 00:50:27.286
Guys, I'm really excited about
spending this weekend together.


00:50:27.354 --> 00:50:29.105
Dad, please,
I'm begging you.


00:50:29.172 --> 00:50:30.873
Let me go to my friend's
house so I can go the party.


00:50:30.941 --> 00:50:33.743
Barb, it's a family trip and
you are coming, too. Let's go.


00:50:33.810 --> 00:50:36.995
Here, get your snorkel.
Let's go, let's go.


00:50:37.063 --> 00:50:38.731
Come on. I feel like
we're forgetting something.


00:50:38.798 --> 00:50:40.899
We have everything, but
the furniture and the dog.


00:50:40.967 --> 00:50:43.319
Look at him.
He's just sitting there!


00:50:43.386 --> 00:50:44.303
I know.


00:50:44.371 --> 00:50:45.804
You think he'll be
okay here alone?


00:50:45.872 --> 00:50:48.073
I think he'll be fine.
He's got food and water


00:50:48.141 --> 00:50:50.109
and I'm having Laura from
down the street look in on him.


00:50:50.176 --> 00:50:51.443
Right. Right.


00:50:51.511 --> 00:50:53.145
I mean, what's the worst that
can happen? He has a party?


00:50:53.213 --> 00:50:55.164
Invites his
girlfriend over?


00:50:55.165 --> 00:50:57.515
Yes and yes!


00:51:00.186 --> 00:51:03.855
Party at the Duke's!
Rager, man! Yeah!


00:51:03.940 --> 00:51:05.891
Jump! Jump! Jump!


00:51:07.126 --> 00:51:10.212
I am a golden dog!


00:51:10.280 --> 00:51:11.514
Canine-ball!


00:51:18.004 --> 00:51:21.273
Looking good, Colby!
Sweet collar, Aurora!


00:51:22.392 --> 00:51:25.043
Yes! Yes!


00:51:25.078 --> 00:51:26.712
My boy, Topaz!


00:51:26.780 --> 00:51:28.047
Marmaduke.


00:51:29.182 --> 00:51:30.882
Chug it! Chug it!


00:51:30.950 --> 00:51:32.050
Go, go, go!


00:51:32.085 --> 00:51:33.619
Chug it, Shasta!


00:51:33.687 --> 00:51:34.719
Ow!


00:51:34.787 --> 00:51:36.221
Sorry, slipped off
the seat again!


00:51:36.289 --> 00:51:38.440
That is
not cool, dude!


00:51:38.508 --> 00:51:39.725
Hey, is this
your party, dude?


00:51:39.793 --> 00:51:41.326
Yeah!


00:51:41.394 --> 00:51:46.498
We're not worthy, we're not
worthy! We love you, man!


00:51:46.566 --> 00:51:50.069
All right! Now it's a
party! Yeah, come on!


00:51:50.136 --> 00:51:51.920
Who let the dogs out?


00:51:51.988 --> 00:51:53.689
Pee-Wee,
hit the Crazy String!


00:51:56.125 --> 00:51:58.010
You're a big hit,
Marmaduke!


00:51:58.078 --> 00:52:01.513
Hey, is it just me, or is it
getting a little out of hand?


00:52:01.581 --> 00:52:03.849
Everyone's having fun,
loosen up!


00:52:04.985 --> 00:52:06.535
Yeah!
Of course, of course!


00:52:06.603 --> 00:52:09.554
No, no, you're right.
Forget what I said.


00:52:13.226 --> 00:52:16.245
Why is everyone always
having more fun than us?


00:52:16.312 --> 00:52:18.597
Because they're not afraid to live?


00:52:18.665 --> 00:52:20.749
And we suck at swimming?


00:52:21.885 --> 00:52:23.952
Great! Okay, now
I'm catching a cold.


00:52:24.020 --> 00:52:25.054
Come on, let's go.


00:52:26.222 --> 00:52:27.356
What do
you smell, girl?


00:52:27.424 --> 00:52:28.807
Trouble.


00:52:28.875 --> 00:52:31.042
Duke! Duke! Duke!


00:52:37.033 --> 00:52:39.384
Hey, dude,
get out of the trash!


00:52:39.452 --> 00:52:41.403
Do I know you
from somewhere?


00:52:41.438 --> 00:52:43.355
Me? Nope.
Never seen you before.


00:52:43.423 --> 00:52:44.690
You sure?


00:52:44.758 --> 00:52:46.207
That tail looks painful.


00:52:46.242 --> 00:52:49.578
Of course I'm sure, man. I've
never even been to a dog park.


00:52:49.645 --> 00:52:50.745
Oops.


00:52:52.632 --> 00:52:54.099
It's so soothing!


00:52:54.167 --> 00:52:56.101
Gordie, no!
No, not on Debbie's rug!


00:52:56.169 --> 00:52:57.552
Whoa, whoa!


00:52:57.620 --> 00:53:00.906
No, no! Hey! Not on the
couch! You raised in a barn?


00:53:02.292 --> 00:53:03.776
No, not the stereo!


00:53:03.844 --> 00:53:05.143
Phil's gonna kill me!


00:53:05.211 --> 00:53:08.948
Looks like a great party.
Now, I'm sorry to interrupt.


00:53:09.015 --> 00:53:10.298
What are you doing here?


00:53:10.366 --> 00:53:11.917
I got a quick question.


00:53:11.985 --> 00:53:14.820
Anyone recognize
this cute little fella?


00:53:14.888 --> 00:53:17.373
The cat from the park
that Marmaduke hazed?


00:53:18.725 --> 00:53:21.660
I recommend the guacamole.
It's dynamite.


00:53:21.728 --> 00:53:23.912
Look at the tail.


00:53:23.947 --> 00:53:26.231
Turns out he lives
here with Marmaduke.


00:53:26.299 --> 00:53:28.667
Or is it Marma-fake?


00:53:36.309 --> 00:53:38.844
First of all, you weren't
invited here, Bosco.


00:53:38.912 --> 00:53:41.880
Leave now and you won't have a
problem. And take Whiskers with you.


00:53:41.948 --> 00:53:43.348
We have
a "no cat" policy.


00:53:43.416 --> 00:53:45.017
Say what?


00:53:45.084 --> 00:53:48.670
Is that right? Then how do you
explain that picture over there?


00:53:48.738 --> 00:53:51.106
Hey, it is that cat.


00:53:51.174 --> 00:53:53.225
Yep, that's it.
That's the cat.


00:53:53.293 --> 00:53:54.693
Let's
get out of here.


00:53:54.761 --> 00:53:56.061
Wait! Wait!


00:53:56.128 --> 00:53:59.982
What's going on? Where
you going? No, no, stay!


00:54:00.049 --> 00:54:02.151
Total poser.
Where are you going?


00:54:02.218 --> 00:54:03.218
Loser!


00:54:03.286 --> 00:54:04.803
He's going, not us!


00:54:04.871 --> 00:54:08.456
Party at the pier!
All right, let's go! Party!


00:54:09.492 --> 00:54:11.526
Is it true, Marmaduke?


00:54:14.230 --> 00:54:16.014
Only most of it.


00:54:16.082 --> 00:54:19.768
You see, in the end,
pedigrees always win.


00:54:19.835 --> 00:54:22.087
And that's the way
it'll always be.


00:54:22.155 --> 00:54:24.807
Enjoy the rest of
your party, mutt.


00:54:25.642 --> 00:54:27.025
Baby, come on.


00:54:28.628 --> 00:54:31.997
Jezebel! He's a liar.
Come on, let's go.


00:54:32.064 --> 00:54:33.866
Hey, Bosco,
wait up!


00:54:36.302 --> 00:54:38.303
Jezebel, wait! I...


00:54:40.857 --> 00:54:43.292
I thought
you were different.


00:54:49.332 --> 00:54:51.350
What just happened?


00:54:51.417 --> 00:54:54.319
I think it's called a colossal
fall from grace, hermano.


00:54:54.387 --> 00:54:55.470
Oh!


00:54:55.538 --> 00:54:57.873
Not to rub margarita salt in the wound,


00:54:58.525 --> 00:55:00.959
but you kind of
deserved it.


00:55:19.629 --> 00:55:21.696
Oh! What have I done?


00:55:29.105 --> 00:55:30.839
Can't wait for the
next family boat trip.


00:55:30.907 --> 00:55:32.441
It was a weekend
on a boat, okay?


00:55:32.509 --> 00:55:33.975
It was a work-end, honey.


00:55:34.044 --> 00:55:35.677
We had to finish
the presentation and...


00:55:35.745 --> 00:55:37.613
What happened?


00:55:37.680 --> 00:55:39.348
Marmaduke?
No.


00:55:40.116 --> 00:55:42.066
Phil.
No!


00:55:42.134 --> 00:55:44.402
I'm up, I'm up.
Where am I?


00:55:45.721 --> 00:55:46.854
Marmaduke!


00:55:47.457 --> 00:55:49.591
I'm up, I'm up.


00:55:49.659 --> 00:55:51.693
Phil, thank God
you're here.


00:55:51.761 --> 00:55:53.762
I had a party.


00:55:53.830 --> 00:55:55.648
I was trying to be a big
shot... Off the couch!


00:55:55.715 --> 00:55:57.182
I just invited
some friends


00:55:57.250 --> 00:56:00.052
and then they invited
friends. It just got crazy!


00:56:00.120 --> 00:56:02.537
Come here, now!
I'm sorry.


00:56:02.605 --> 00:56:05.440
Phil, I really could
use a hug right now.


00:56:05.992 --> 00:56:07.225
Bad dog!


00:56:07.293 --> 00:56:08.593
Phil, no! Phil,
I'm trying to explain!


00:56:08.661 --> 00:56:09.545
Phil, stop it.


00:56:09.612 --> 00:56:11.063
Just give me
a chance to...


00:56:11.130 --> 00:56:12.881
Phil, I said I was sorry.


00:56:20.673 --> 00:56:22.174
The PETCO pitch.


00:56:22.742 --> 00:56:24.610
Oh, Marmaduke.


00:56:26.028 --> 00:56:27.629
Ooh!
Uh-oh, Daddy.


00:56:30.950 --> 00:56:34.036
I don't care if it's raining,
I'm done. He can sleep outside.


00:56:34.103 --> 00:56:35.837
Perfect, that will
solve everything.


00:56:35.905 --> 00:56:39.174
We'll just leave him chained up in
the backyard for the next 10 years.


00:56:39.242 --> 00:56:40.742
Or maybe
we give him away.


00:56:41.493 --> 00:56:43.512
You did not
just say that.


00:56:43.547 --> 00:56:45.531
He refuses to
listen to me!


00:56:45.598 --> 00:56:48.967
It's just an option we haven't
explored yet, that's all I'm saying.


00:56:49.035 --> 00:56:51.103
I don't understand
you sometimes.


00:56:51.171 --> 00:56:52.696
Look around you, Deb.


00:56:52.731 --> 00:56:54.222
He destroyed our home!


00:56:54.290 --> 00:56:55.741
No, he didn't!


00:56:55.808 --> 00:56:58.627
Our home is us. It's
you and me and the kids.


00:56:58.695 --> 00:57:00.662
It doesn't matter
where we are.


00:57:02.481 --> 00:57:05.617
This move did not work out
the way I hoped it would.


00:57:05.752 --> 00:57:07.720
The only way this move
was ever gonna work out


00:57:07.787 --> 00:57:10.038
is if we were
in it together.


00:57:10.106 --> 00:57:12.273
You seem to have
lost sight of that.


00:57:13.192 --> 00:57:15.593
Everything I do
is for us.


00:57:15.661 --> 00:57:17.028
I worked my butt
off this weekend,


00:57:17.096 --> 00:57:19.931
and once again,
that dog screwed it up!


00:57:19.999 --> 00:57:23.635
He's a dog, Phil! He
doesn't know any better.


00:57:23.737 --> 00:57:25.804
You want him to
sleep outside, fine.


00:57:25.872 --> 00:57:29.224
He has a backyard,
you have a couch.


00:57:29.859 --> 00:57:31.659
Really?
Really.


00:59:41.440 --> 00:59:44.475
You know what?
It's not that easy.


01:00:09.902 --> 01:00:12.287
Nobody ever
puts in a cat door!


01:00:15.124 --> 01:00:16.824
Hey, you must be Mazie.


01:00:16.859 --> 01:00:20.295
Tell the hipster giant I'm not
interested in his peace offering.


01:00:20.330 --> 01:00:23.415
He's gone. He got busted with
Phil and had to sleep outside.


01:00:23.483 --> 01:00:25.450
He ran out the back gate
about an hour ago.


01:00:25.518 --> 01:00:28.220
Oh, great. He has
zero street smarts.


01:00:28.287 --> 01:00:29.520
Where you going?


01:00:29.588 --> 01:00:31.356
To find that big doofus!


01:00:31.423 --> 01:00:34.242
I'd go myself,
but I can't get wet.


01:00:37.279 --> 01:00:38.546
Yeller.


01:00:43.852 --> 01:00:46.388
Oh! You crazy,
wonderful dog.


01:00:50.159 --> 01:00:53.645
He acts like it's a great
big romp, doesn't he, Travis?


01:00:53.679 --> 01:00:56.147
Crazy as a bullbat.


01:00:56.215 --> 01:00:59.050
He's a heap more dog than
I ever had him figured for.


01:01:06.426 --> 01:01:08.126
None of the strays at
the pound have seen him.


01:01:08.194 --> 01:01:09.694
He's not at
the dog park either.


01:01:09.762 --> 01:01:11.163
No luck here.


01:01:11.230 --> 01:01:13.731
I made a huge mistake wearing
the bumble-bee sweater.


01:01:13.799 --> 01:01:15.417
It's way too absorbent!


01:01:19.055 --> 01:01:21.156
It's raining cats and us!


01:01:21.223 --> 01:01:23.442
You guys head home, I'm
gonna look a little longer.


01:01:23.509 --> 01:01:25.677
We can't leave you
out here alone!


01:01:25.744 --> 01:01:27.762
It's too dangerous!


01:01:31.801 --> 01:01:33.234
Okay, on second thought,
you have fun.


01:01:33.302 --> 01:01:34.636
You do that whole thing.
Good luck.


01:02:13.409 --> 01:02:15.143
Chupadogra?


01:02:15.210 --> 01:02:18.262
Who are you? And what
are you doing here?


01:02:18.330 --> 01:02:20.248
Please don't hurt me!


01:02:20.315 --> 01:02:22.350
You're a big boy.


01:02:22.417 --> 01:02:26.354
Good. The small ones ain't
got enough meat on their bones.


01:02:27.523 --> 01:02:29.056
Please don't hurt me!
I'm sorry, I...


01:02:31.543 --> 01:02:33.027
Are you okay?


01:02:33.095 --> 01:02:34.996
I'm more than all right.


01:02:37.666 --> 01:02:39.034
Sorry to bother you.


01:02:39.101 --> 01:02:42.737
Hey, what's a dog like you
doing out here, anyways?


01:02:42.805 --> 01:02:44.906
You're no stray.


01:02:44.974 --> 01:02:46.641
I ran away from home.


01:02:48.061 --> 01:02:52.164
So, you think running's the answer? Huh?


01:02:54.717 --> 01:02:56.818
I don't even know
what I'm doing anymore.


01:02:56.886 --> 01:03:01.756
I acted like a big-shot and
lost all my friends, my family.


01:03:01.824 --> 01:03:06.411
Listen, this bag of bones you're
looking at used to be something special.


01:03:07.146 --> 01:03:09.281
I was the alpha dog.


01:03:09.348 --> 01:03:13.385
Left my home to go run the
pack. And man, did I run it.


01:03:14.387 --> 01:03:16.487
Till they turned on me.


01:03:16.555 --> 01:03:21.025
Now I live out here alone
dodging trains and dogcatchers.


01:03:21.093 --> 01:03:24.996
Rest assured, compadre,
there ain't a day goes by


01:03:25.064 --> 01:03:27.499
when I don't think about
waking up in a warm bed


01:03:27.567 --> 01:03:31.035
and spending the day
with the folks who love me.


01:03:31.104 --> 01:03:32.837
The real me.


01:03:33.606 --> 01:03:35.206
Go home.


01:03:35.274 --> 01:03:38.777
Something tells me it ain't
too late for the real you.


01:03:40.212 --> 01:03:42.880
Thank you, Buster.


01:03:46.735 --> 01:03:51.589
Been a long time
since anybody called me that.


01:03:52.124 --> 01:03:53.291
Thanks.


01:03:54.577 --> 01:03:55.744
What's that?


01:03:55.811 --> 01:03:57.628
It's the pound.


01:03:57.696 --> 01:03:59.731
Go on, get out of here.
Get!


01:03:59.798 --> 01:04:01.883
What about you?
You're sick!


01:04:01.918 --> 01:04:05.570
Yeah, that's right, baby.
I'm one sick puppy.


01:04:05.638 --> 01:04:07.222
Go on, go!


01:04:13.345 --> 01:04:15.596
Let's make this easy,
old timer.


01:04:15.664 --> 01:04:17.015
What fun would that be?


01:04:18.384 --> 01:04:20.017
No, no! No!


01:04:57.740 --> 01:04:59.774
Debbie, you got
to listen to me.


01:04:59.842 --> 01:05:02.276
Marmaduke is missing. He's
been gone since last night!


01:05:02.344 --> 01:05:04.562
We're talkative this
morning! Go eat your num-nums.


01:05:07.032 --> 01:05:08.132
Hey, Deb.


01:05:08.200 --> 01:05:10.084
Did you leave these
on the table in there?


01:05:10.152 --> 01:05:11.519
What are you
talking about?


01:05:12.655 --> 01:05:16.024
Barb, I read the text. And...


01:05:17.209 --> 01:05:18.810
Is that really
how you feel?


01:05:20.929 --> 01:05:22.380
Honestly?


01:05:24.834 --> 01:05:26.133
Yeah.


01:05:28.520 --> 01:05:31.406
Hey, Bri.


01:05:31.474 --> 01:05:33.375
You never went to
soccer practice, did you?


01:05:35.944 --> 01:05:40.080
I didn't want to disappoint you,
but you weren't really listening.


01:05:47.306 --> 01:05:49.356
Where's Marmaduke?


01:05:49.391 --> 01:05:51.793
In the backyard,
sweetie.


01:05:51.861 --> 01:05:53.995
No, he's not. I thought
he was upstairs with you.


01:05:54.063 --> 01:05:55.162
No.


01:05:57.216 --> 01:05:59.050
Marmaduke!
Marmaduke!


01:05:59.118 --> 01:06:02.220
The side gate's open. You didn't
let him back in last night?


01:06:02.287 --> 01:06:03.420
No.


01:06:03.455 --> 01:06:05.323
That's what
I've been saying.


01:06:05.391 --> 01:06:07.008
He'll be back, right?


01:06:08.277 --> 01:06:09.811
He could get
hit by a car.


01:06:09.879 --> 01:06:10.795
Honey, anything
could happen


01:06:10.862 --> 01:06:12.630
because we don't know
how long he's been gone.


01:06:12.631 --> 01:06:14.282
I just wanted him to
sleep in the backyard,


01:06:14.350 --> 01:06:17.218
I didn't want him
to run away. God!


01:06:17.286 --> 01:06:19.354
I got this
presentation.


01:06:20.589 --> 01:06:24.492
Guys, if I don't
nail this, I'm done.


01:06:25.277 --> 01:06:27.045
Just go.
We'll find him.


01:06:27.112 --> 01:06:29.680
You put her in the car seat, and
you get Marmaduke's leash, okay?


01:06:29.748 --> 01:06:31.098
Wait.


01:06:36.755 --> 01:06:38.255
We'll all go find him.


01:06:38.323 --> 01:06:39.607
Now you're
talking, amigo.


01:06:42.160 --> 01:06:46.297
Come on, where am I? Just give
me one little scent of home.


01:06:46.299 --> 01:06:48.116
Marmaduke! Come on, buddy. Marmaduke!


01:06:48.184 --> 01:06:50.034
Come on, boy.
Marmaduke!


01:06:50.102 --> 01:06:52.437
Okay, that was the
neighborhood. So, where else?


01:06:52.505 --> 01:06:54.138
The beach. He could be at the beach.


01:06:54.140 --> 01:06:55.640
Okay, the beach and
maybe the dog park?


01:06:55.707 --> 01:06:58.009
You guys, I'm texting
everybody I know.


01:06:58.076 --> 01:06:59.761
What if he's
at the pound?


01:06:59.829 --> 01:07:02.113
Come on, come on, give me
something I can recognize.


01:07:02.180 --> 01:07:04.682
One landmark,
one little scent.


01:07:08.954 --> 01:07:10.337
What do you mean,
"What does he look like?"


01:07:10.405 --> 01:07:13.307
He's a Great Dane! He's huge.
He's twice the size of your dog.


01:07:13.375 --> 01:07:16.477
Come on,
give me a scent.


01:07:16.544 --> 01:07:19.547
One more funky
little Marmaduke smell.


01:07:21.817 --> 01:07:23.618
Come on, not today!


01:07:28.557 --> 01:07:30.391
Hi, Don. Winslow,
where the heck are you?


01:07:30.459 --> 01:07:32.327
You were supposed to
be here an hour ago!


01:07:32.394 --> 01:07:34.712
I'm sorry, Don. Uh...


01:07:34.780 --> 01:07:37.348
We still haven't
found Marmaduke


01:07:37.416 --> 01:07:39.433
and I just don't think
I'll make it in today.


01:07:39.501 --> 01:07:41.269
Don't worry about
coming in today,


01:07:41.336 --> 01:07:43.254
because you're fired,
Winslow!


01:07:57.870 --> 01:07:59.170
Mazie?


01:07:59.872 --> 01:08:01.389
Mazie? Mazie!


01:08:02.124 --> 01:08:02.990
What is this?


01:08:03.058 --> 01:08:04.959
It looks like
a water main broke.


01:08:08.130 --> 01:08:09.530
There he is!
Wait! I'm coming!


01:08:09.597 --> 01:08:11.499
Honey! Honey!
Right there, look!


01:08:11.500 --> 01:08:13.467
Kids, never do this.


01:08:16.805 --> 01:08:18.873
Marmaduke!
Where was he, Brian?


01:08:18.940 --> 01:08:20.642
He was up there.


01:08:20.709 --> 01:08:22.910
Marmaduke! Here, go wait
in the car with your mom.


01:08:23.212 --> 01:08:24.261
Marmaduke!


01:08:28.316 --> 01:08:29.818
Mazie!


01:08:29.885 --> 01:08:31.385
Marmaduke!


01:08:31.820 --> 01:08:33.071
Mazie!


01:08:33.138 --> 01:08:36.006
Where have you been? I've
been looking all over for...


01:08:37.425 --> 01:08:39.210
Mazie! No!
What?


01:08:39.277 --> 01:08:40.594
Mazie!
Marmaduke!


01:08:40.662 --> 01:08:42.163
No, no,
don't let me fall!


01:08:42.231 --> 01:08:43.998
Marmaduke!
Come on, let's go!


01:08:44.066 --> 01:08:46.383
Come on, buddy!
Marmaduke, where are you?


01:08:46.451 --> 01:08:48.570
Somebody, help! Mazie!


01:08:48.637 --> 01:08:49.821
No! Marmaduke!


01:08:49.889 --> 01:08:51.972
Mazie! Mazie!


01:08:52.007 --> 01:08:53.925
Hey, Marmaduke,
come on, let's go!


01:08:53.993 --> 01:08:55.442
Stay back.
Phil, help me!


01:08:55.510 --> 01:08:57.345
Get away from me!
Hey, stay back!


01:08:57.829 --> 01:08:59.029
Geronimo!


01:08:59.097 --> 01:09:00.264
Marmaduke, no!


01:09:01.584 --> 01:09:04.035
That's my dog. That's my dog in there!


01:09:06.105 --> 01:09:07.872
Look, that was my dog.
Can somebody help me?


01:09:07.940 --> 01:09:09.340
Can you please help me
get him out of there?


01:09:09.408 --> 01:09:11.476
There's a catch basin
about two blocks down.


01:09:11.543 --> 01:09:13.194
We need
a water rescue, over.


01:09:13.229 --> 01:09:14.545
Help!


01:09:20.602 --> 01:09:22.603
Marmaduke!


01:09:22.671 --> 01:09:24.288
Mazie!


01:09:24.356 --> 01:09:26.607
Where are you, Marmaduke?


01:09:28.410 --> 01:09:29.844
I can't do this!


01:09:29.912 --> 01:09:31.012
Hold on.
I'm coming, Mazie!


01:09:31.079 --> 01:09:32.163
Help me! Help me!


01:09:32.230 --> 01:09:34.114
Somebody, help! Mazie!


01:09:34.182 --> 01:09:36.483
Marmaduke!
Help! Help!


01:09:36.551 --> 01:09:39.037
Help, help,
don't let me fall!


01:09:39.505 --> 01:09:40.688
Mazie!


01:09:44.593 --> 01:09:46.160
Go! Go! Go! Go!


01:09:47.696 --> 01:09:49.881
All right.
Get me two more guys here.


01:09:52.735 --> 01:09:54.084
What are we
gonna do?


01:09:54.152 --> 01:09:55.386
Just hold on.


01:09:55.453 --> 01:09:56.654
I'm gonna
figure this out.


01:09:59.691 --> 01:10:01.960
Anything?


01:10:02.027 --> 01:10:03.394
Wait, wait,
I think I hear someone.


01:10:03.429 --> 01:10:04.678
Down here!


01:10:06.982 --> 01:10:09.183
I think
he's gonna help us.


01:10:09.251 --> 01:10:11.535
Yeah. We're right here.
What should we do?


01:10:11.620 --> 01:10:13.871
I found them, over.
Come on, girl.


01:10:13.939 --> 01:10:15.906
I don't think I can make it! Come here.


01:10:15.974 --> 01:10:17.075
No, I can't!


01:10:17.142 --> 01:10:18.492
Come on, girl,
it's okay.


01:10:18.560 --> 01:10:20.644
Listen to him.
Mazie, you can do this.


01:10:20.679 --> 01:10:22.580
You can do it, right here.
I don't think I can make it!


01:10:22.648 --> 01:10:23.548
Come on, girl,
just jump.


01:10:23.616 --> 01:10:25.583
Come on.
You can do it.


01:10:26.585 --> 01:10:29.404
Good, you got it!
Take her first.


01:10:29.438 --> 01:10:31.805
Go ahead. Come on, it's your turn. Jump!


01:10:31.873 --> 01:10:33.674
Me? No. I can't do it,
I'm too big!


01:10:33.742 --> 01:10:35.542
Come on,
you can do it!


01:10:35.610 --> 01:10:36.994
What's that noise?


01:10:37.062 --> 01:10:38.195
Marmaduke, look out!


01:10:38.263 --> 01:10:39.497
You got to come, boy.
Hurry!


01:10:39.564 --> 01:10:41.031
You got
to be kidding me!


01:10:41.099 --> 01:10:43.084
Come on, boy! Hurry!


01:10:43.152 --> 01:10:44.401
Grab me!
You better grab me now!


01:10:48.490 --> 01:10:50.057
What's happening?
Jam it! Jam it!


01:10:50.125 --> 01:10:51.025
Get him out!


01:10:53.345 --> 01:10:54.628
Up, up, up!
Let's go!


01:10:54.696 --> 01:10:56.197
You guys, easy.


01:11:04.189 --> 01:11:05.890
Easy!
There he is.


01:11:05.958 --> 01:11:07.524
We got him up. Guys!


01:11:07.593 --> 01:11:09.060
He's out.
He's out.


01:11:09.127 --> 01:11:10.327
Where's the other one?


01:11:10.996 --> 01:11:11.996
Where's my dog?


01:11:13.098 --> 01:11:14.465
I'm sorry.


01:11:14.533 --> 01:11:16.234
The water was
moving too fast.


01:11:16.268 --> 01:11:17.368
I lost him.


01:11:20.973 --> 01:11:23.041
We're not gonna give up.
Where does this go?


01:11:23.076 --> 01:11:24.442
The aqueduct,
it's just down there.


01:11:26.312 --> 01:11:28.078
Go with him. Go.


01:11:51.920 --> 01:11:53.154
Marmaduke!


01:12:05.384 --> 01:12:06.484
Marmaduke!


01:12:06.551 --> 01:12:08.936
Phil, help!
Get me. Phil!


01:12:15.277 --> 01:12:16.610
Marmaduke!


01:12:17.595 --> 01:12:18.495
Help!


01:12:19.814 --> 01:12:21.014
Get me, Phil!


01:12:22.284 --> 01:12:23.250
Marmaduke!
Help!


01:12:27.488 --> 01:12:29.707
Marmaduke!
I'm right here, buddy.


01:12:29.775 --> 01:12:32.193
Grab here, Phil!
Grab on to this.


01:12:35.230 --> 01:12:37.264
Phil! Phil,
where are you? Phil!


01:12:37.332 --> 01:12:39.166
Phil! Phil!


01:12:42.554 --> 01:12:44.222
Thank goodness
you're okay!


01:12:45.891 --> 01:12:46.924
Marmaduke!


01:12:46.992 --> 01:12:49.277
Right here, come on!


01:12:49.344 --> 01:12:50.911
I can't...
I'm too scared.


01:12:50.979 --> 01:12:52.179
Right here.
Come on.


01:12:54.700 --> 01:12:55.983
Oh, no!


01:13:00.972 --> 01:13:03.741
How did it come
to this, Phil?


01:13:03.809 --> 01:13:06.494
It started with a bath,
and now look at us.


01:13:06.561 --> 01:13:08.162
We can do this.


01:13:09.298 --> 01:13:10.965
I'm not gonna
let you go.


01:13:11.032 --> 01:13:12.800
I can't do it.


01:13:13.468 --> 01:13:14.702
I promise.


01:13:15.687 --> 01:13:17.454
Let go,
and I'll catch you.


01:13:17.522 --> 01:13:19.223
I love you, buddy.
Come on!


01:13:19.290 --> 01:13:22.443
Phil, I've been waiting since
Kansas to have you say that.


01:13:22.510 --> 01:13:23.610
Come on, let's go!


01:13:23.678 --> 01:13:24.945
You can do it, buddy.


01:13:25.847 --> 01:13:27.181
Right here. Come on.


01:13:27.249 --> 01:13:28.749
Trust me.


01:13:28.816 --> 01:13:30.768
I trust you.
Here I come!


01:13:32.437 --> 01:13:34.121
Atta boy, buddy.
Come on!


01:13:34.189 --> 01:13:35.990
Right here.
Swim to me.


01:13:36.057 --> 01:13:38.092
Let's go. Come on.
Phil, help!


01:13:38.159 --> 01:13:40.444
Get me. Phil, get me!


01:13:44.266 --> 01:13:46.134
All right,
come on! I got you.


01:13:47.002 --> 01:13:48.619
I love you, buddy.


01:13:48.687 --> 01:13:51.105
Thank God, you got me! We did it! Yes!


01:13:51.173 --> 01:13:53.558
You got me, Phil!
You got me!


01:13:53.625 --> 01:13:54.992
You're safe, buddy.


01:13:55.060 --> 01:13:58.162
Those aren't tears,
it's just a little water!


01:13:58.230 --> 01:13:59.063
Good boy.


01:13:59.131 --> 01:14:00.581
Harness coming down!


01:14:04.570 --> 01:14:06.570
I still hate water!


01:14:34.933 --> 01:14:37.467
I know you're not
gonna understand a word of this


01:14:37.535 --> 01:14:41.438
but I've never been so happy to see
that big, ugly face in my whole life.


01:14:44.442 --> 01:14:47.044
I'm done pretending
to be a top dog.


01:14:48.446 --> 01:14:51.448
A real top dog
looks out for his family.


01:14:51.516 --> 01:14:54.117
And you are my family.


01:14:54.185 --> 01:14:56.921
That's it,
I can't stand it anymore.


01:14:56.989 --> 01:14:58.772
I'm gonna give him
the tongue.


01:14:59.408 --> 01:15:01.125
That's a good boy!


01:15:02.961 --> 01:15:05.129
I know, I know!


01:15:05.196 --> 01:15:07.364
I've been on this
crew nine years.


01:15:07.432 --> 01:15:11.201
And that, my friend,
is some pretty strong stuff.


01:15:11.753 --> 01:15:13.054
Come on, buddy!


01:15:13.121 --> 01:15:14.104
Honey?


01:15:14.172 --> 01:15:15.306
Dad!
Dad!


01:15:15.373 --> 01:15:16.890
Hey, guys!


01:15:16.958 --> 01:15:18.392
Are you okay?
Hi, Dad.


01:15:18.460 --> 01:15:20.394
I'm okay. I'm okay. I'm just
a little wet, that's all.


01:15:20.462 --> 01:15:22.079
Marmaduke!
Look who I found!


01:15:22.147 --> 01:15:23.180
Marmaduke!


01:15:23.248 --> 01:15:24.799
Oh, yeah!
Get a little Marmaduke.


01:15:24.866 --> 01:15:27.034
Let me wrap my
paws around you!


01:15:27.102 --> 01:15:28.869
We missed you.


01:15:28.937 --> 01:15:29.971
Hi, there.


01:15:30.038 --> 01:15:31.872
Hi!
Okay, you're all wet!


01:15:31.940 --> 01:15:34.675
Gosh, I love you guys
so much.


01:15:34.743 --> 01:15:37.411
This is all my fault. I
never asked what you wanted.


01:15:37.479 --> 01:15:40.114
I've just been trying
so hard to make this work


01:15:40.181 --> 01:15:43.067
that I had no idea
you were so unhappy.


01:15:43.134 --> 01:15:45.202
I guess what I'm
trying to say is


01:15:45.270 --> 01:15:47.171
I think we should
move back to Kansas.


01:15:47.372 --> 01:15:49.457
What?
Move back to Kansas?


01:15:49.524 --> 01:15:52.960
Kansas? Uh-uh. Toto
ain't going nowhere, papi.


01:15:53.027 --> 01:15:54.712
That's crazy talk, Dad.


01:15:54.779 --> 01:15:56.596
Hey, Brian!


01:15:56.631 --> 01:15:59.917
Dude, we got it all on tape.
We're putting it on YouTube!


01:15:59.985 --> 01:16:01.835
Sweet!


01:16:01.903 --> 01:16:04.004
It's good to see you,
Bri. What are you doing?


01:16:04.072 --> 01:16:05.573
Brian, who are
your friends?


01:16:05.974 --> 01:16:07.391
They're just some kids
I met at the skate park.


01:16:07.459 --> 01:16:09.626
They're pretty cool.
Hey, boys!


01:16:09.694 --> 01:16:10.845
Hi.
Sup?


01:16:13.632 --> 01:16:14.665
Hey, Barbara!


01:16:14.700 --> 01:16:16.617
Hey, what's Hasselhoff
doing here?


01:16:16.685 --> 01:16:19.803
Bodie? You came.


01:16:19.871 --> 01:16:22.456
Yeah, I came as soon as
I got your text message.


01:16:22.524 --> 01:16:23.908
Is everybody okay?


01:16:23.976 --> 01:16:28.429
Yeah, everything's
much better now.


01:16:28.497 --> 01:16:30.831
Those were some pretty
sick moves, Mr. Winslow.


01:16:31.433 --> 01:16:33.167
Thank you, Bodie.


01:16:33.234 --> 01:16:35.636
No worries, Phil.


01:16:35.704 --> 01:16:37.471
It's Mr. Winslow.


01:16:38.139 --> 01:16:39.373
Yes, sir.


01:16:42.327 --> 01:16:44.895
What do you think, babe?


01:16:44.963 --> 01:16:48.532
I don't know. I like
it here. I think we fit here.


01:16:48.600 --> 01:16:49.867
We fit in the house.


01:16:50.852 --> 01:16:53.187
We don't fit in
that company car.


01:16:56.007 --> 01:16:57.742
I just missed you.


01:17:01.413 --> 01:17:03.046
Looks like we're home.


01:17:05.984 --> 01:17:08.518
Looks like the family
landed on their feet.


01:17:08.587 --> 01:17:11.405
There's just one more thing
I got to take care of.


01:17:12.457 --> 01:17:13.758
Check it out.


01:17:13.825 --> 01:17:15.876
Here goes nothing.


01:17:15.943 --> 01:17:17.861
What the heck is he doing? Is he crazy?


01:17:17.929 --> 01:17:19.730
Fight! Fight! Fight!


01:17:23.568 --> 01:17:24.935
Don't just stand there,
do something!


01:17:25.003 --> 01:17:26.870
I am.
I'm standing my ground!


01:17:27.005 --> 01:17:29.473
What's up, Marmadukey?


01:17:29.474 --> 01:17:31.342
You here to
exact revenge?


01:17:31.410 --> 01:17:34.645
Actually, no, Bosco.
I'm here to thank you.


01:17:35.246 --> 01:17:38.382
Thank me? For what?


01:17:38.449 --> 01:17:40.935
For showing me
how wrong I was.


01:17:42.471 --> 01:17:44.004
I don't care what
everyone thinks of me


01:17:44.071 --> 01:17:46.407
'cause it doesn't matter
if you're big or small


01:17:46.474 --> 01:17:48.692
or a pedigree
or a mutt.


01:17:48.760 --> 01:17:50.560
We're all just dogs.


01:17:50.628 --> 01:17:53.264
And that's the way
the park should be.


01:17:53.331 --> 01:17:57.234
So I'm gonna sit down and
claim this spot for all the dogs


01:17:57.269 --> 01:18:01.138
who don't think they have
what it takes to be over here.


01:18:03.108 --> 01:18:05.575
Sup? Yeah.


01:18:05.643 --> 01:18:09.138
You gotta be kidding me.
You're kidding me, right?


01:18:09.173 --> 01:18:12.633
Does everyone here have
rabies-induced insanity?


01:18:12.701 --> 01:18:14.818
This is sacred turf.


01:18:14.886 --> 01:18:17.487
It's just for pedigrees.


01:18:17.555 --> 01:18:19.239
Well, not anymore.


01:18:19.307 --> 01:18:22.075
You know what? You're all
just mutts. All of you!


01:18:22.143 --> 01:18:23.844
Let's go, Jezebel.


01:18:23.911 --> 01:18:26.830
I think everyone
should sit here, too.


01:18:26.898 --> 01:18:29.367
I'm done taking your
spit on my head, Bosco.


01:18:29.434 --> 01:18:31.869
Go find somebody else to drool
on. We're through with you!


01:18:31.936 --> 01:18:33.370
Come have a seat, fellas.


01:18:33.437 --> 01:18:34.838
It's lovely up here.


01:18:35.940 --> 01:18:38.024
I can see forever!


01:18:38.092 --> 01:18:40.127
Fine, have it
your way, losers.


01:18:40.194 --> 01:18:41.662
I'll remember this.


01:18:41.730 --> 01:18:43.314
Payback's gonna be a...


01:18:43.382 --> 01:18:45.799
Bee! Bee! Ahhh!


01:18:47.535 --> 01:18:49.769
Victory!
Victory is ours!


01:18:49.837 --> 01:18:51.238
The Duke's our boy!


01:18:51.306 --> 01:18:54.458
Huh! Looks like I'm not the
only one terrified of bees.


01:18:54.526 --> 01:18:55.976
Bees are scary.


01:18:57.245 --> 01:18:58.779
Listen...


01:18:58.847 --> 01:19:01.065
I don't know how to say this
without hurting your feelings...


01:19:01.132 --> 01:19:02.666
Shh!


01:19:02.734 --> 01:19:07.204
I'll be fine. It's time to finally
stand on my own four legs for a while.


01:19:07.271 --> 01:19:09.606
Besides,
we'll still be friends.


01:19:09.674 --> 01:19:12.242
Ouch! I hate it
when girls say that.


01:19:15.713 --> 01:19:17.281
Mazie?


01:19:17.866 --> 01:19:19.266
Wow.


01:19:22.687 --> 01:19:24.571
Hey, check it out.


01:19:24.639 --> 01:19:27.774
Looking good
in the pink.


01:19:27.842 --> 01:19:29.677
What are you
waiting for? Go!


01:19:29.744 --> 01:19:31.211
Mazie, wait up!


01:19:33.531 --> 01:19:34.698
Oh, hey!


01:19:37.268 --> 01:19:39.085
You look amazing!


01:19:39.153 --> 01:19:42.205
I feel like
a fluffy monstrosity.


01:19:42.273 --> 01:19:46.126
Listen, I wanted to say how sorry
I am for the way I've been acting.


01:19:46.194 --> 01:19:49.329
I was a real jerk,
and you didn't deserve it.


01:19:49.397 --> 01:19:53.050
I think my brain just turned
into an Afghan Hound for a while.


01:19:53.118 --> 01:19:54.167
No offense.


01:19:54.235 --> 01:19:55.336
I totally heard that.


01:19:56.805 --> 01:19:58.972
It takes a big dog
to admit that.


01:19:59.925 --> 01:20:01.091
Yeah, I...


01:20:01.559 --> 01:20:02.960
What?


01:20:03.027 --> 01:20:05.395
Your eyes. You have
really pretty eyes.


01:20:05.464 --> 01:20:07.731
And I never had
a chance to tell you.


01:20:09.134 --> 01:20:10.900
Thanks!


01:20:10.968 --> 01:20:12.736
Your fur's
really nice, too.


01:20:14.038 --> 01:20:15.405
Winslow!


01:20:15.473 --> 01:20:18.408
Oh! I wonder what ever
happened to that PETCO deal.


01:20:20.228 --> 01:20:25.115
Winslow! Winslow? There you
are, I've been looking for you.


01:20:25.183 --> 01:20:26.383
I thought I was fired.


01:20:26.451 --> 01:20:28.151
Don't be so sensitive.


01:20:28.219 --> 01:20:30.387
Any man that chooses
his dog over his career


01:20:30.455 --> 01:20:32.872
is a man I want
working for me.


01:20:32.940 --> 01:20:36.476
Besides, have you seen the video of
you rescuing Marmaduke on YouTube?


01:20:36.544 --> 01:20:37.811
Nah.


01:20:37.879 --> 01:20:40.313
Six hundred and eighty-two
thousand hits so far.


01:20:40.381 --> 01:20:41.298
We got PETCO!


01:20:41.365 --> 01:20:43.400
Are you serious?
Totally!


01:20:44.452 --> 01:20:45.919
We're gonna sell
a lot of dog food!


01:20:45.987 --> 01:20:47.037
Wow!


01:20:47.105 --> 01:20:48.805
Come on, walk with me.
We got work to do.


01:20:48.873 --> 01:20:49.940
I can't.


01:20:50.007 --> 01:20:51.241
Why?


01:20:51.309 --> 01:20:52.943
'Cause I made plans
with my family.


01:20:53.011 --> 01:20:57.414
Who? Oh. All right.
All right, tomorrow.


01:20:57.966 --> 01:20:59.333
Monday.


01:21:00.752 --> 01:21:02.719
Monday. Deal.


01:21:03.088 --> 01:21:04.021
Deal.


01:21:05.172 --> 01:21:07.474
Don't push it, okay?


01:21:08.326 --> 01:21:10.528
Okay, I'm just
spit-balling here


01:21:10.595 --> 01:21:13.631
but what if the dogs
could talk to each other?


01:21:14.666 --> 01:21:15.966
I don't really buy it.


01:21:17.636 --> 01:21:19.637
What if they
could dance?


01:21:24.475 --> 01:21:25.609
# Hey!


01:21:29.681 --> 01:21:32.365
# What I like about you


01:21:32.433 --> 01:21:35.686
# You really know
how to dance


01:21:35.754 --> 01:21:38.204
# When you go up, down,
jump around


01:21:38.272 --> 01:21:40.524
# Think about true romance


01:21:43.060 --> 01:21:45.579
# Keep on whispering
in my ear


01:21:45.646 --> 01:21:47.982
# Tell me all the things
that I want to hear


01:21:48.049 --> 01:21:50.125
# 'Cause it's true


01:21:52.270 --> 01:21:53.604
What's up, boys?


01:21:53.672 --> 01:21:55.188
That's what
I like about you.


01:21:56.357 --> 01:21:58.759
# That's what
I like about you


01:22:03.397 --> 01:22:04.397
# Hey!


01:22:09.137 --> 01:22:10.220
Hey!


01:22:12.573 --> 01:22:14.474
That's what
I like about you.


01:22:19.897 --> 01:22:20.797
# Hey! #


01:22:24.636 --> 01:22:26.102
It's still pretty
rough. What do you think?


01:22:26.170 --> 01:22:28.037
I love it!
Great job.


01:22:28.105 --> 01:22:29.539
Thanks, Deb.


01:22:36.330 --> 01:22:39.599
Wait for it.
Wait for it.


01:22:42.003 --> 01:22:44.646
Oh! Marmaduke!
What did you eat?


